{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are","id":1557471,"title":"\"Nephandi Are Not Playable!\" Except They Are.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-11T09:50:05-08:00","id":1557471,"title":"\"Nephandi Are Not Playable!\" Except They Are.","content":"So, apparently, the writers of the Nephandi book made a huge fuss about how they would never create a player's guide for the Nephandi, and they were supposed to be exclusively antagonists. However, I have discovered a flaw in their plan. Said flaw being the fact that magic in the <b>Ascension</b> setting is pretty much an open sandbox, where you're free to do anything you want, so long as you have a convincing way to fit it within consensus.<br /> <br /> <br /> With that in mind, it should actually be quite easy to make a Nephandus into a playable character. Whether that be a reflavored Hollow One using their magic for evil, or a corrupted Verbena who kidnaps children to steal their youth. There's all kinds of ideas you could draw from to make this work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T11:41:33-08:00","id":1557472,"title":"","content":"I mean, there isn't really a flaw in their plan. The game doesn't support playable Nephandi.<br /> <br /> They are well aware that people &quot;can&quot; play Nephandi against the developers' wishes.<br /> <br /> In a way, you're kinda making their point (and most specifically Saytros Brucato's point, as he's the most adamantly against playable Nephandi): playing Nephandi isn't about just playing evil mages that do scummy thing. Nephandi aren't Hollowers on &quot;evil&quot; mode. They're not mages that kill to extend their own lives.<br /> <br /> Voormas, one of the big bads of the game, is not a Nephandi and he's trying to destroy the world by destroying death itself because ultimately he's too afraid of dying to let it happen to him. He's a mass murderer running a cult of mass murderers, and still isn't as evil as the Nephandi are (even if he's very evil and very immediately dangerous in a fashion that needs stopping ASAP).<br /> <br /> Playing Nephandi as if they were normal PCs generally means diluting them into something that removes their role in the setting, or means you're playing characters with far worse morals than Voormas; and while most posters here don't like being told they can't play such a monster, there is a justifiable question of why we would really want to, Yes, we're playing the WoD, but every WoD game has antagonists you're not supposed to play even if you can figure out how to do it within the mechanical rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T12:35:01-08:00","id":1557477,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Nephandi are evil mages, but evil mages don't need to be (and for the most part aren't) Nephandi<br /> <br /> A &quot;corrupted Verbena who kidnaps children to steal their youth&quot; isn't necessarily a Nephandus. It's just a terrible person that has the means to do something a lot of old horrible humans would wish to be able to do.<br /> <br /> Some depictions of Nephandi show them jumping to the fiery arms of the demons they summon as if they didn't cared about their lives or well being. Ofc not all Nephandi are like this, but I would wager the &quot;Ideal Nephandi&quot; doesn't care about their health other than as a medium to better fuck up the world. Voormass was <i>opposed </i>by Nephandi because of his horrific quest for immortality, after all.<br /> <br /> Nephandi are - at their conceptual core - inverted mages whose Avatars search for cosmic annihilation. How they as humans relate to this dark enligthenment it's going to colour their goals.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, &quot;a corrupted Verbena who kidnaps children to steal their youth&quot; <i>could </i>be a Nephandus. Or she <i>could </i>just be an evil witch that doesn't care about the children, and believes herself above retaliation. There's nothing particularly Nephandic in that, <i>per se</i>. <hr /><br /> I think that a Nephandi character should be developped thinking about being the &quot;dark reflection of mages&quot;. But what does that mean? .<br /> <br /> <b>It's not a normal expression of Evil</b>. Mages are already horribly evil people as a collective w/o being Nephandi. The Technocracy, the protectors of humanity, are all stronlgly bassed arround SciFy distopies about control (they have the Room 101 - for crying out loud). The Traditions like to see themselves as the better version of all of their groups, all with lofty ideals, but in practice they can't enforce this morality because their internal structure it's too focused on allowing freedom to actually enforce any kind of morality - and thus you have all ethical-council Etherites traveling with umbrella shields to protect themselves from the Mad Scientists menacing them with orbital death rays -<br /> <br /> For evil's sake - think about that: You can have a mad scientists that creates literal &quot;death rays&quot; to menace the innocent. And they're not Nephandi. They're a core option to play.<br /> <br /> Nephandi aren't like that. Nephandi being the &quot;dark refection&quot;, in my opinion it's more like this:<br /> <br /> Mages are special people supernaturally driven to make themselves and the world <i>better</i> - for whatever that means (like: for an egoist mage, a better world could be one where he can do whatever he wants). Mages are people that can't be wrong, that don't accept to be wrong, not even if the world it's against their ideas.<br /> <br /> Nephandi are the opposite of that: supernaturally driven to destroy and debase themselves and the world. They're nihilists that don't care about being right, but do care about proving everyone else it's wrong. They're almost <i>ontologicaly evil,</i> as they express the dissolution of anything ethical with the ultimate goal of perpetuating suffering 'til the universe gives up and turns back to oblivion.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it much more simply (and canon, too). They're the &quot;some people just want to see the world burn&quot; type<br /> <br /> Like a textbook example could be a &quot;road to hell it's paved with good intentions&quot; character that's apparently peaceful and helpfull because his way to make people fall it's to make them go to extremes in their ideals, so, give them rope to hang themselves - then make sure they get to a point of no return where it's &quot;compromise your morals or everything you fought for it's gonna crumble&quot;. Then, if possible, make sure it crumbles anyway.<br /> <br /> That's a Nephandi <hr /><br /> Personally, I wouldn't go for it:<br /> <br /> One in a normal chronicle would be a whole nother level of PvP, even above what's normal on Vampire or WoD. You have one player actively wanting to destroy the literal spirits of everyone else on the table.<br /> <br /> That's not just being evil - you can have an evil character that's also loyal to their own and can work as part of a group. The Sabbat it's cartoonishly evil, but in their own way they are noble and make sense. They can be noble monsters and are fiercely protective of their own.<br /> <br /> A Nephandi betraying the group it's the best thing that could happen to the group. A *loyal* Nephandi goalpost it's to make everyone ideals and goals to be broken and twisted 'til they accept to have their Avatar Inverted. Maybe a young Nephandi that's trying to figth against it could be more playable, but there's no concrete support for this on the books<br /> <br /> And what about an &quot;all nephandi&quot; group? I think that's less polemical. I imagine it would be a story that's all about carefully destroying the world I built, on a conceptual level. I think it's an OK concept, tho not one I care about exploring right now - and all the players can be on the same page on this.<br /> <br /> <b>SO:</b><br /> <br /> The RPG police isn't going to hunt you down for playing Nephandi. It's totally doable. BUT it's not true that the &quot;evil wizard concept&quot; and the Nephandi concept are one and the same<br /> <br /> I made this wordly thread mostly to say that you can play all sort of villanous, evil, wizards and don't be a Nephandi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":".  clarifications 01-11-2026, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T13:50:27-08:00","id":1557479,"title":"","content":"More to the point, <b>Book of the Fallen</b> doesn't say &quot;thou shalt not&quot;; it says &quot;there will be consequences if you do&quot;. Not in the sense that the Canon Ninjas will swoop in and steal your books, but rather in the sense that playing something like a Nephandus takes a toll on the player. That's why the book aims less at enabling Nephandic player characters and more at enabling the reader to identify and confront the sort of abuse that the Nephandi represent. <br /> <br /> Put another way, the message is that this is dangerous, and should be treated with utmost care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T14:53:27-08:00","id":1557480,"title":"","content":"Not all Nephandi are bent on cosmic annihilation. In fact, only the <i>&quot;Exies&quot;</i> seem to be wholly on board with that idea. Other groups within their order seek to reshape the world into something that is more in line with their twisted desires.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mammonites</b> will do literally anything to turn a profit, and damn the consequences. Not exactly seeing the point in making money, if you have nothing to spend it on.<br /> <br /> <b>Goat Kids</b> are more obsessed with indulging their vices, to the point where the other factions dismiss them as a joke. Despite the fact they are supposedly the largest faction of Nephandi.<br /> <br /> <b>Heralds of the Basilisk</b> are trying to create an A.I God who will reward them for their service, while punishing those who did not aid in its creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Black Man</b>, first and presumed leader of the K'llasshaa, was promised by the outer lords that if he brought them to earth, they would elevate him above all other beings. A promise which they end up keeping during one of the potential end times scenarios, as The Black Man ends up becoming the planet's new dark overlord.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------<br /> <br /> As for the evil Hollow One idea, I was just using that as an analogy. I said you could reflavor them, because the Hollow Ones don't really have an established paradigm that falls in line with the Traditions. They make up their own approach to magic, which you could say draws upon Qlippothic magic to function properly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T15:13:38-08:00","id":1557482,"title":"","content":"Another issue (and I have no idea what the M20 material says on the matter) is that some of the earlier material (I would have to look up where and don't have my books handy) occasionally implied that the Nephandi may (I stress <i>may</i>) effectively be puppets of the beings they serve, lacking real free will. If true, this would mean that in a game focused on imposing one's own will on reality, they are incapable of doing so, instead only being the tools something else is using to manipulate and eventually erase reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T15:28:03-08:00","id":1557483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557482#post1557482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another issue (and I have no idea what the M20 material says on the matter) is that some of the earlier material (I would have to look up where and don't have my books handy) occasionally implied that the Nephandi may (I stress <i>may</i>) effectively be puppets of the beings they serve, lacking real free will. If true, this would mean that in a game focused on imposing one's own will on reality, they are incapable of doing so, instead only being the tools something else is using to manipulate and eventually erase reality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've heard something similar to that effect, in that when one passes through a Caul, they are confronted with a physical manifestation of everything they consider to be wrong in the world. They then must kneel before it and pledge to serve it willingly and whole heartedly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then again, the aforementioned Black Man would put this tidbit of lore under scrutiny, as he was serving the Outer Lords in the interest of becoming the most powerful being on earth.<br /> <br /> Then there's the whole inverted tree of wisdom aspect, which (allegedly) culminates in the Nephandus emerging out the other side as some kind of malevolent deity. I don't know if it's true or not, but some of the Nephandi art does appear to have them undergoing a profound transformation of some kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T15:57:55-08:00","id":1557484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557482#post1557482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another issue (and I have no idea what the M20 material says on the matter) is that some of the earlier material (I would have to look up where and don't have my books handy) occasionally implied that the Nephandi may (I stress <i>may</i>) effectively be puppets of the beings they serve, lacking real free will. If true, this would mean that in a game focused on imposing one's own will on reality, they are incapable of doing so, instead only being the tools something else is using to manipulate and eventually erase reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that is fairly consistent across the editions is that there are effectively two kinds of Nephandi beyond specific classifications based on practices and entities they might deal with:<br /> <br /> 1) There are the &quot;evil mages&quot; that couldn't hide among the other factions and are recruited by the Nephandi. Those that don't show potential for true Descension are used as tools. Either by the Nephandus that recruited them, or offered to some other dark being. These are implied to be the vast majority of the Nephandi that get caught and killed by the other factions; disposable pawns that harm the world while active but can't be used against the fully committed fanatics behind them.<br /> <br /> 2) Then there are the true believers in Descension. Some might be young and reckless, but older Nephandi that know the battle is a long one keep them safe enough to grow into the ranks of the most destructive mages. The older members of this group are the things that make even the most powerful mages in the Traditions, Technocracy, and the Disparates fear for the future. These Nephandi might have started by making deals with devils, but they have the power to render such contracts as meaningless as the Nephandi view reality itself. Early stepping stones to gain power, but things that can be moved beyond in time. Some never pledged themselves to any specific entity or cause. They will, over a long enough period of time, reclaim their agency because not even the cosmic horrors of the Outer Dark realms can keep them bound forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T16:15:40-08:00","id":1557486,"title":"","content":"The Book of Mirrors, the original (2nd ed) Mage Storytellers Guide, flat out stated in no uncertain terms that <i>all</i> of the Nephandi are actively working toward the annihilation of reality. They are effectively a virus working to kill its host. (The revised Book of Madness reiterates this.) Things like greed, hedonism, power, and the like are nothing more than lures. Gateways to Descension, nihilism, and the death of the soul.<br /> <br /> Also, the entities they serve, regardless of what mask they wear, are the Neverborn, the embodiments of Oblivion from outside reality that seek the end of everything. This isn't any sort of conjecture; It is an objective fact of the setting stated clearly in the Book of Mirrors and repeated in later material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T16:21:36-08:00","id":1557487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557486#post1557486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Book of Mirrors, the original (2nd ed) Mage Storytellers Guide, flat out stated in no uncertain terms that <i>all</i> of the Nephandi are actively working toward the annihilation of reality. They are effectively a virus working to kill its host. (The revised Book of Madness reiterates this.) Things like greed, hedonism, power, and the like are nothing more than lures. Gateways to Descension, nihilism, and the death of the soul.<br /> <br /> Also, the entities they serve, regardless of what mask they wear, are the Neverborn, the embodiments of Oblivion from outside reality that seek the end of everything. This isn't any sort of conjecture; It is an objective fact of the setting stated clearly in the Book of Mirrors and repeated in later material.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is that information provided out of character, or in character? Because in character means we have to take the unreliable narrator aspect into account.<br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, Demon flat out says that the pagan deities the Verbena worship are actually demons themselves. Which means the Verbena are involved in demon worship, whether they know it or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T19:15:32-08:00","id":1557494,"title":"","content":"Demon says a lot of things that run completely contrary to the established settings of the other game lines... it's really not a great choice to bring up unless crossover across multiple game lines is already in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T01:10:44-08:00","id":1557498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557494#post1557494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon says a lot of things that run completely contrary to the established settings of the other game lines... it's really not a great choice to bring up unless crossover across multiple game lines is already in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Ratkin said, the other settings are written from an in character perspective, meaning they are unreliable narrators at best.<br /> <br /> And considering demons were there at the creation of the world, and even helped take part in it, I'd say they're a better authority on such matters.<br /> <br /> They literally grow more powerful by harvesting faith from their cultists. So passing themselves off as pagan deities sounds like something they would definitely do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T01:24:22-08:00","id":1557499,"title":"","content":"Agreeing with the above. If you want to play an evil Vampire, play an evil Vampire. That Vampire could be a Baali, or an Evil Bloodline, but Brujah can be perfectly Evil on their own. If you want to play an evil Changeling, you've got plenty of options. A Seelie Troll who is prepared to obey ANY order from the House they serve is 100% compatible with the Court, and would be considered &quot;good&quot; by many in the setting. You don't have to play a Thallain. And if you want to play an evil Mage, play an evil Mage. They don't have to be a Nephandus.<br /> <br /> All this to say, for a PC you're better off playing chooses-to-be-evil, as that comes with some tension, as opposed to evil-by-default, which generally speaking has less room to explore. Not that you can't tell an interesting story about a Baali or a Thallain, of course, it's just quite unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T03:31:44-08:00","id":1557502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557498#post1557498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Ratkin said, the other settings are written from an in character perspective, meaning they are unreliable narrators at best.<br /> <br /> And considering demons were there at the creation of the world, and even helped take part in it, I'd say they're a better authority on such matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons are the most unreliable of all in the modern day, because the Abyssal Prison literally warped their minds and memories into fractured messes before the process of possessing a human host made them struggle even more to remember the truth of the primordial past.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, there are more important issues:<br /> <br /> 1) Mage is Mage first, and part of the wider WoD second; as are all the games. In Mage, the Verbena are not demon cultists just for not belonging to an Abrahamic based religious background. In Mage &quot;demon&quot; is a vague term that can mean dozens of different types of entities and isn't exclusive to the PCs from Demon: the Fallen.<br /> <br /> 2) There are mechanics for getting your powers from demonic sources. Unless a mage is using those rules, they're not worshiping demons to get their powers even if their Focus directly involved demon-worship. A normal mage's power comes from their own beliefs and will. Powers from other sources use specific mechanics to indicate that. You don't have to take such powers to play a Verbena.<br /> <br /> 3) It's not fun for forum conversations, or just playing the games, to be playing one game only to get &quot;well actually...&quot; about what's said in another game.<br /> <br /> 4) Even more so, it's extremely uncool to do so to make an otherwise pluralistic game into one that explicitly favors some real world faith traditions over others. A lot of people play these games because they come from backgrounds that have been demonized by colonialism and so on, but the games don't punish you for that and in fact empower you for doing so. Coming back in and saying such players are wrong because demons say that non-Christians are all actually deluded demon worshipers so that must be true is not a great way to treat everyone that isn't a Christian and likes the games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They literally grow more powerful by harvesting faith from their cultists. So passing themselves off as pagan deities sounds like something they would definitely do. </div> </div> </div>Canonically they did it to non-pagan people too. The are literal former angels and all. Passing themselves off as not &quot;former&quot; is pretty easy for them. Only further making it a fairly silly thing to get into for a Mage thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T03:45:07-08:00","id":1557503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557502#post1557502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 4) Even more so, it's extremely uncool to do so to make an otherwise pluralistic game into one that explicitly favors some real world faith traditions over others. A lot of people play these games because they come from backgrounds that have been demonized by colonialism and so on, but the games don't punish you for that and in fact empower you for doing so. Coming back in and saying such players are wrong because demons say that non-Christians are all actually deluded demon worshipers so that must be true is not a great way to treat everyone that isn't a Christian and likes the games.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... that's literally how World of Darkness is presented, though!<br /> <br /> It's not a question of if the Abrahamic faiths are true, it's pretty much outright confirmed. The end times even culminate with demons being released from Hell, and God coming back to cleanse the world because of how messed up everything is. Lucifer, the actual, biblical devil is walking the earth as we speak.<br /> <br /> Wraith presents us with the knowledge that while other versions of the afterlife do exist, they are corrupted versions of what humanity believed them to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Imbued were granted divine powers, and a holy mandate from God (or his messengers) to go forth and commit an ethnic cleansing of every supernatural culture they could find, because they didn't like the fact they were practicing magic / communing with spirits. Funnily enough, the Celestial Choristers are included in that list. So I'm not sure what's going on there?<br /> <br /> <br /> Is it cool? No, I guess not. But it's still accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 01-12-2026, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T08:29:31-08:00","id":1557508,"title":"","content":"As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> said, it's not that you <i>can't</i> play a Nephandus, it's that playing has direct consequences in the table that you are playing. Nephandi, beyond the many justifications for their existence in-universe, are abusers and corrupters <i>per excellence</i>, even the aforementioned <i>Book of The Fallen</i> has an entire section explaining and contextualizing in the Mage setting different kinds of abuse, be it emotional, religious, sexual, etc. Playing one in your table is bound to make someone uncomfortable and break boundaries, even in the case that all of you are playing Nephandi, since the &quot;society&quot; of the Fallen is predicated on the notion of &quot;eat or be eaten&quot;.<br /> <br /> I agree that not every Nephandi is a omnicidal maniac. Just like any Mage when discussing the topic of Ascension, Ascension (or in this case, Descension), can be personal or global. But even in your examples, for the perspective of maintaining cohesion in a party of player characters, it's gonna get ugly really quick: for the Mammonites, since it's profit beyond any morals, you can sell out your party enough times that the only way to deal with that character is open PVP; for the Goat Kids, indulgence with no limits can get really, <i>really dark</i> (I don't think I have to spell it out here); for the Heralds, you are describing a cult-like logic that, sure if you aid us in our dark god's ascension we will help you, but a shred of doubt about the coming of the Basilisk warrants severe punishment, I cannot see a party of characters of diverse motivations working without eveyrone converting to the Heralds. And besides, although you describe these examples as ones that do not search for a destruction of reality itself, I think that's a superficial read, since profit, indulgence and a cult-like mentality for technology have pervasive consequences in society at large that a Mage game table surely would explore.<br /> <br /> But beyond all that, I agree with other posts here: all these concepts can work without the Nephandi and in much better ways. A Mage which values profit above all else, but don't want to see the world end, is not a Mammonite, but a Syndicate agent that, while ruthless in driving profits with hypereconomics, still recognizes the primacy of the Technocracy's mission and will finance ventures from other conventions (an ideia presented in <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i>); a Mage which values indulgence, even to extreme extents, but doesn't want to corrupt other people to the point of abuse is a concept appropriate for an Ecstatic with a Left-Hand way of Magick; a Mage that searches for the construction of an AI god could be an Iterator close to being a Marauder but that still holds the ideia that this will bring a kind of Utopia. All of these concepts have a shade of evil, but none of them comes close to how the Nephandi are portrayed. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> is right that to view the Nephandi as just evil, like any other typical villain group of the WoD, is to dillute their importance in the setting, to the point that it's better to scrap them entirely from your chronicle.<br /> <br /> Another aspect I wanted to add to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>'s argument is that beyond the consequences to other players, I believe that playing a Nephandus is not a good thing for the player playing it, an opinion that if I'm not mistaken is shared by Brucato. To play any character is to immerse yourself in that character's motivations and worldview, and sure, some tabletop players don't hold the acting part of roleplay to such a high bar, but even then we try to at least think from our characters perspectives. In order to play a Nephandus, you - the player, need to hold a collection of motivations while roleplaying that is gonna affect you in some way, shape or form. I'm not saying that this will make anyone playing a Nephandus an automatic Evil Wizard IRL, it's just a game afterall, but I think that like any other piece of fiction, it can emotionally affect you in subtle ways.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","user":"Agrat","date":". 01-12-2026, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T10:23:47-08:00","id":1557519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557487#post1557487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If I'm not mistaken, Demon flat out says that the pagan deities the Verbena worship are actually demons themselves. Which means the Verbena are involved in demon worship, whether they know it or not.</div> </div> </div> </div> Leaving Demon demons vs Mage demons aside, *even* worshipping demons doesn't make you a Nephandi. Infernalism: Path of Screams goes to a great extent explaining this, and even states that Nephandi are against selling their souls to demons. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is that information provided out of character, or in character? Because in character means we have to take the unreliable narrator aspect into account. </div> </div> </div>I can confirm the writteup on book of mirrors it's OOC, intended to Storytellers. It's pretty good, I think. It goes a bit on deeper than just &quot;The End, close the book&quot;. It could also be &quot;just&quot; utter devastation of unimaginable proportions to the point you can say, the universe was destroyed (like how &quot;destroying earth&quot; doesn't need to mean that there's not even an atom of dirt left).<br /> <br /> This point has been repeated a lot of times, and it's very coherent between editions. The end of the Nephandic path is: Destruction/Apocalypse. It is their mage path. But that doesn't mean that's the only thing they can desire. A Nephandic Avatar it's hell bent on Descencion. Arguably more so than regular Avatars are on Ascencion - considering there isn't a single good Nephandi.<br /> <br /> This is the ultimate destruction. As &quot;human&quot;, however, I would imagine Nephandi can get still get clogged in this path and not reach its end, or misinterpret it. So, you have Nephandi that want to get rich, or kill babies for a reason.<br /> <br /> However, annihilation is still the road they thread as a Mage. Whenever they raise Arete they're commiting to it. And thus a Nephandi that wants to get rich it's still pushed to do so in the most destructive way possible, rather than the most practical. While a particular Nephandi personal goals migth be different from &quot;end everything&quot;, they're always going to be &quot;coloured&quot; by this drive. It's what makes them special.<br /> <br /> A villan that *doesn't* have desires, urges and visions driving them to create a Hell on Earth as the bare minimum, it's probably better represented by someone who isn't a Nephandi. <hr /><br /> A little about the Black Man. Most of what we know about this character it's from an end of the world scenario that didn't happened. That and an incredibly old book from an era where Oracles/Aswadim were a a bit different from today. But I still think he supports most of what I have said.<br /> <br /> 1) He it's totally an agent of dissolution<br /> <br /> The Black Man severely punished Nephandi for daring to so much as have a *faction name*. Because that brings unification, and the Path it's dissolution. Imagine what he would think about them having *subsects*. Or being actually invested as part of &quot;a group&quot; But, of course, he's an Aswadim. Less enligthened Nephandi may opt to associate for self benefit. But this IS being &quot;less enligthened&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2) Sure, he doesn't go and personally kick every atom out of existence, but he does cause a level of destruction that's both conceptual and impossible to imagine, destroying the Axis Mundi, the entity that that gives structure to the universe and sepparates it's layers, to let the Outer Dark from before Creation in. &quot;The order of Creation it's broken&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which has consecuences that seem very hard to survive for non mages, such as people being unable to give birth, water becoming blood and venom. The end of the world has a hopeful note in that it can be reversed by mages figthing against it, but, really that's all of it.<br /> <br /> To say he just wants to &quot;rule the world&quot; sort of undermines the fact that this ruling comes from causing such an uspeakable destruction that the Things from Before Creation (from before God say &quot;let there be ligth&quot;) can roam arround and feel at home.<br /> <br /> And this is just one idea about what could be the end goal of Nephandi: Hell on Earth (Wyrm Apocalypse and Neverborn being the other two possible explanations of what Descencion is, AFAIK).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-12-2026, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T11:24:49-08:00","id":1557520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557503#post1557503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... that's literally how World of Darkness is presented, though!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to belabor this any further, so if you want me to get much deeper into this instead of refocused on the specifics of the thread, please tag me in a new thread or DM me.<br /> <br /> But no, it isn't. Mage has never been presented this way and predated Demon by 19 years. Mage did not alter its presentation after Demon was released (esp. not with M20).<br /> <br /> The WoD has never, ever, been presented as a cohesive whole. It's been presented as close enough you can cross over if you want to, but always distinct enough that every game line works within itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T12:09:53-08:00","id":1557522,"title":"","content":"The issue isnt really that you can't play a Nephandi it's that you shouldn't. They don't really have free will and suffer from reduced agency so their isn't much of a character arc there.<br /> I've seen one played well and that was a dramatic unveiling appropriately timed with agreement between player and GM. Usually they're dull as dirt on the table if messy and unpleasent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T16:31:51-08:00","id":1557527,"title":"","content":"I will say that I had a great deal of fun playing a reformed infernalist who got cold feet before being sent to the Cauls and turned stool pigeon on everything he knew about the Nephandi. It made for a very dramatic start for the first session, beginning <i>in media res</i> with his former demonic familiar trying to blow him up in his sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T10:23:10-08:00","id":1557782,"title":"","content":"My two questions are why would you do that at all, and why would that be a good idea.<br /> <br /> 1. Normal Mages can be evil, no problem. They can enslave people, eat children, corrupt spirits, blaspheme against the sanctity of life and death, all the nine yards. No need to make a Nephandus;<br /> <br /> 2. A Nephandus is characterized by the Path of Descension however your ST defines it. It's not about them being evil people, its about their Avatar guiding them to universal unraveling;<br /> <br /> 3. The writers didn't say their reason was not to give rules for playing Nefandi. They actually did gave them, more clearly than any previous edition (which weren't completely without those), they said they wouldn't make a book focused on exploring the roleplaying aspects of playing a Nefandus;<br /> <br /> 4. You're right, it isn't hard. It's just bad. Boring for some people to begin with, at least as far as long term playing goes. But also a very bad place to explore for many players.<br /> <br /> If you still want to go ahead, though, it's your problem. You'll either end up with a char that's a Nephandus in name, only, or a character that's very hard to play, for dubious return, at your own risk.<br /> <br /> For no mechanical challenge, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T02:41:44-08:00","id":1557796,"title":"","content":"My two cents: when a Nephandi's psychological drive, enforced by their mangled Avatar, is to pursue Ontological Evil, purely for its own sake, a Nephandus PC will always be <i>less interesting</i> than a PC who is merely a bad person.<br /> <br /> Regular humans do evil for all manner of reasons. Practical, emotional, ideological, or personal. All can be fascinating to deconstruct and examine. A witch who steals the youth from children? *Chef's kiss*. Classic! They could do it for vanity, or out of fear of death, or as a desperate attempt to buy time to accomplish some goal. Do they feel guilt over it? Or do they not care? Feel entitlement? Is it a revenge or jealousy thing?<br /> <br /> A Nephandus who steals the youth of children does it for precisely two reasons: 1) for the lulz, and 2) to prolong their life so they can do more evil for the lulz.<br /> <br /> Having complex motivations or approaches is nice to have for a Nephandi, but hardly required. Any reasons they give are just after-the-fact rationalizations for what the Nephandus wanted to do anyway: sow pain, madness, ruin, death, and destruction. Descent is not a rational motivation, and goes against everything humans stand for.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to another point: you shouldn't play a Nephandus because it's <i>bad for you</i>. <br /> <br /> It's very unhealthy to inhabit the persona of a being opposed to every aspect of human decency, even within the context of a roleplaying game. To run them as a character, and at every juncture ask the question &quot;what's the absolute worst thing I could do in this situation?&quot;. And where the only reason your character restrains their impulses is because it would be unwise or risky. A fact the character resents for thwarting their <a href=\"https://dresdencodak.com/2009/01/27/advanced-dungeons-and-discourse/\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Dark Kantian&quot; categorical imperative</a> to do Evil, regardless of utility.<br /> <br /> To constantly and willingly plot against even your fellow PCs (including Nephandi ones). To deceive, manipulate, abuse, and betray them, in the immediate term and over the long term. Not because your PC pursues an understandable goal that necessitates the deception, but because your PC seeks to maximize harm and cruelty. To be the ultimate asshole player, the ultimate &quot;That Guy&quot; at the table. Disrupting everyone else's fun because &quot;it's what my character would do&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's not fun. Not for the rest of the group, and probably not much for you either. It's exhausting, and probably not a good headspace to occupy for long campaigns.<br /> <br /> At least when the Storyteller roleplays the Nephandi, it's largely in the abstract until the PCs finally meet them face to face. At sporadic intervals, and with the express intent that the PCs will ideally <i>kill this mother-fucker</i> and end their evil. With a Nephandi PC, you have to effectively BE that mother-fucker, and try to make them work.<br /> <br /> Is it any wonder, then, that White Wolf's creatives (especially Brucato) didn't want to provide the tools to do that? They didn't want to give players a rope to hang themselves with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T04:35:22-08:00","id":1557797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557782#post1557782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My two questions are why would you do that at all, and why would that be a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, when you examine the World of Darkness cosmology in its entirety, across each of the different splats and how they relate to the metaplot, returning the universe to Zero Sum is not just rational, but downright merciful.<br /> <br /> To put it simply, the universe of WoD has become so FUBAR, that you may as well just wipe the slate clean and start over.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> God is an egotistical tyrant, who cursed humanity out of spite when we chose knowledge over blind submission.<br /> <br /> The Triat have gone insane and become radicalized in pursuing their roles. Even the threat of Gaia blowing herself up only managed to deter them for a short while, before Wyrm realized <i>&quot;oh, yeah, I'm destruction incarnate.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The Shining Realms of the Underworld are a lie, as they've fallen to corruption and are now under the control of a bunch of power hungry wraiths that pass themselves off as gods.<br /> <br /> Charon went completely insane with power and fucked up Wraith society so badly, that in a final moment of clarity, he decided to sacrifice himself and let the remaining Wraiths clean up the mess he made.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy are bullshitting you when they say they want to keep humanity safe. What they actually want is absolute control over the world. FFS, they even implant their agents with cerebral chip that monitor their thoughts and regulate their behavior. One of the story blurbs even features a Technocrat accidentally shorting out his chip and regaining his free will long enough to chronicle his experience.<br /> <br /> Not only did the Technocracy help create the Nazi regime, as part of their plan to establish a One Nation, One Culture system, but they also created <b>Threat Null</b> that is slowly making its way towards earth as we speak. And when it gets here, it's going to assimilate all of us, like the freaking BORG.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fae, the spiritual embodiments of humanity's capacity for dreams, creativity and imagination are dying, because of how crushingly banal our society has become. Don't get me wrong, I'm fully aware the Fae aren't exactly perfect in their relationship with humanity. But it's still depressing to know they're going extinct.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> And the list just kind of keeps going on like that.<br /> <br /> Mistake, after mistake, after mistake.<br /> <br /> Everything has gone to shit, so why not pull the plug while you still have the chance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T04:56:55-08:00","id":1557798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557796#post1557796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd hesitate to say the Nephandi are hard coded to be PVP. While it's true that turning on your allies for the sheer entertainment value is an evil action, it overlooks the fact the Nephandi have a structural hierarchy. Which implies at least some level of organized cooperation between them.<br /> <br /> <br /> The end result of <i>Descension</i> is nearly as mysterious as that of <i>Ascension</i>. With some believing that it results in the complete destruction of all reality, and others claiming that it leads to a <b>Dark Apotheosis</b>, in which you become an alien god of your own making. It's even speculated that the <b>Outer Lords</b> may in fact be Nephandi from previous universe who managed to complete this transformation.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Qlippothic realms are also speculated to be the remains of previous universes that fell to the Nephandi's machinations. Which, if that is true, proves the Nephandi have done not only done this dance many times throughout history, but it also proves that some Nephandi seek to reshape the universe, instead of destroy it completely.<br /> <br /> <br /> Once again, the Outer Lords make good on their promise to The Black Man, by elevating him to the status of most powerful being on earth during the end times, and he ends up becoming the planet's new ruler. Why would a Nephandi care about ruling the planet, if his goal is to destroy it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 01-21-2026, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T05:55:30-08:00","id":1557799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd hesitate to say the Nephandi are hard coded to be PVP. While it's true that turning on your allies for the sheer entertainment value is an evil action, it overlooks the fact the Nephandi have a structural hierarchy. Which implies at least some level of organized cooperation between them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some level of organized cooperation it's certainly possible, but Nephandi really do need to consider their PvP if they want to suirvive even among them &quot;pals&quot;. They can have ranks, yeah, but <i>respecting</i> them it's a different matter. Nephandi are very well known for betraying each other at the smallest chance.<br /> <br /> On Descencion, since you like to use the Black Man as an example, it's stated that the order between the Aswadim it's entirely based on power and fear. You can make the other Aswadim turn on the Black Man if you manage to convince them they have a chance to defeat him. And if they do, they will turn on each other soon after. That's allegedly one of the ways to reverse Descencion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The end result of <i>Descension</i> is nearly as mysterious as that of <i>Ascension</i>.With some believing that it results in the complete destruction of all reality, and others claiming that it leads to a <b>Dark Apotheosis</b>, in which you become an alien god of your own making. </div> </div> </div>It's not really necessary to be a Nephandus, much less to Descend, to become a Dark God of your Own Making, tho - just look at Mikaboshi. Godhood it's a relatively easy path for mages of all stripes - and if you're a dark mage, you're going to become a dark god.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once again, the Outer Lords make good on their promise to The Black Man, by elevating him to the status of most powerful being on earth during the end times, and he ends up becoming the planet's new ruler. Why would a Nephandi care about ruling the planet, if his goal is to destroy it? </div> </div> </div>Once again, Descencion brought in such devastation that life on Earth it's basically unsustainable. It's a good thing for them that death no longer exists as a separate state (no longer a separation between the Dark Kingdoms and Earth). They now rule over a hellscape where everything alive it's in a constant agony that death offers no relief from.<br /> <br /> Nephandi didn't *atomized* the world, but they did destroy and defaced it to the point where one could turn your question around: If Nephandi goal was to rule over the world, then why had they to destroy it first?.<br /> <br /> Technocracy hadn't to do that in THEIR end, and they did got to rule the world all the same. It's either &quot;skill issue&quot;, or maybe, just maybe, all that destruction and horror was the goal all along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-21-2026, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T06:49:25-08:00","id":1557800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557799#post1557799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nephandi didn't *atomized* the world, but they did destroy and defaced it to the point where one could turn your question around: If Nephandi goal was to rule over the world, then why had they to destroy it first?.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe because they wanted the world to be made in their own image, rather than somebody else's? :-)<br /> <br /> That's like tracing over somebody else's work and then taking credit for it.<br /> <br /> Anyways, the point is that evil mages are possible from both sides. But one considers evil to be a means to an end, while the other sees evil as the end itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T16:00:33-08:00","id":1557814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, the point is that evil mages are possible from both sides. But one considers evil to be a means to an end, while the other sees evil as the end itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. From a narrative standpoint, I think their peculiar approach to the concept of evil it's what makes the faction distinct more than the specific things they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T19:40:13-08:00","id":1557821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557797#post1557797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put it simply, the universe of WoD has become so FUBAR, that you may as well just wipe the slate clean and start over.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no &quot;starting over&quot; with a Nephandus. Just plain <i>over. </i>All the talk about becoming an &quot;Outer God&quot;, &quot;becoming Leviathan&quot;, is just hogwash to continue convincing themselves that there is an escape from their choice of entering the Caul and condemning themselves to Oblivion. In fact, this lie is reiterated throught <i>Book of The Fallen. </i>Take for example the entry card in page 33, <i>Dogs Don't Actually Eat Dogs, </i>taking aiming at the very notion that the &quot;eat or be eaten&quot; common to all Nephandic Paradigms is even remotely applicable to &quot;human nature&quot;.<br /> <br /> Besides that, it has been said in this thread that converging differents events from the very patch-like metaplot of WoD can shape how an <i>individual game line</i> should be played is bound to contradict something to the spirit of that individual game line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557797#post1557797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mistake, after mistake, after mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may be so bold, that's not a phrase that can describe just the World of Darkness. That's just history, baby. One mistake after another, just turn on the news to see atrocities the world over. But humanity still collectively wakes up and goes on living. To take a phrase from another piece of fiction, a dialogue from Melina in Elden Ring: &quot;<i>However ruined this world has become, however mired in torment and despair. Life endures. Births continue. There is beauty in that, is there not?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557797#post1557797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything has gone to shit, so why not pull the plug while you still have the chance?</div> </div> </div> </div>...Well, you play a <i>Mage</i>. One of the messages of this game is that no matter the situation, <i>you are not helpless</i>. You literally have the power to change Reality.<br /> <br /> But I will let the very first paragraphs of M20 Corebook (p. 18) answer that one:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Magick lives.<br /> <br /> The Art of Change never went away. Though the age<br /> of sorcerers has faded to mythology, magick holds a real and<br /> vibrant role in the world we know.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t think so? Look around you. We fly over oceans and look<br /> across time. The distance between Dallas and Tokyo can fit in your<br /> pocket. You could craft whole worlds out of numbers on a screen, or<br /> visit Africa without leaving your chair. If that\u2019s not magickal, what is?<br /> <br /> Magick isn\u2019t witches on brooms or demons conjured in<br /> the night. It can be, but it isn\u2019t limited to that. Magick is the<br /> force of possibility\u2026 and now, more than perhaps ever before,<br /> it seems as though all things are possible.<br /> <br /> And yet we\u2019re told that the age of miracles is over. We\u2019re<br /> living in the End Times, a hopeless grind where novelty is just<br /> another pop-up ad. We\u2019ve been set against one another in a<br /> round-robin game of trivial pursuits. The best we can hope<br /> for, we are told, is a big house and a warm bed and a bunch<br /> of money in the bank. So sit the fuck down, shut the fuck up,<br /> have your TV and a Big Mac and think you\u2019ve got it made.<br /> <br /> <i>Bullshit.</i><br /> <br /> Wake up.<br /> <br /> Your future\u2019s on the table.\u200b </div> </div> </div>And for good measure, M20 Corebook, p. 20:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Above all other things, Mage is about giving a damn. While<br /> other folks are hopeless or content enough to accept what<br /> they\u2019ve been given, mages change the picture. They disagree,<br /> often violently, about what that picture should look like, but<br /> apathy\u2019s not in their nature. The Awakening won\u2019t let them sit<br /> still and accept the world as it is.\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-22T01:29:09-08:00","id":1557825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agrat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557821#post1557821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no &quot;starting over&quot; with a Nephandus. Just plain <i>over. </i>All the talk about becoming an &quot;Outer God&quot;, &quot;becoming Leviathan&quot;, is just hogwash to continue convincing themselves that there is an escape from their choice of entering the Caul and condemning themselves to Oblivion. In fact, this lie is reiterated throught <i>Book of The Fallen. </i>Take for example the entry card in page 33, <i>Dogs Don't Actually Eat Dogs, </i>taking aiming at the very notion that the &quot;eat or be eaten&quot; common to all Nephandic Paradigms is even remotely applicable to &quot;human nature&quot;.<br /> <br /> Besides that, it has been said in this thread that converging differents events from the very patch-like metaplot of WoD can shape how an <i>individual game line</i> should be played is bound to contradict something to the spirit of that individual game line.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If I may be so bold, that's not a phrase that can describe just the World of Darkness. That's just history, baby. One mistake after another, just turn on the news to see atrocities the world over. But humanity still collectively wakes up and goes on living. To take a phrase from another piece of fiction, a dialogue from Melina in Elden Ring: &quot;<i>However ruined this world has become, however mired in torment and despair. Life endures. Births continue. There is beauty in that, is there not?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...Well, you play a <i>Mage</i>. One of the messages of this game is that no matter the situation, <i>you are not helpless</i>. You literally have the power to change Reality.<br /> <br /> But I will let the very first paragraphs of M20 Corebook (p. 18) answer that one:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And for good measure, M20 Corebook, p. 20:</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>1</b> - Except that their kind of is. Wyrm, Wyld and Weaver have been doing their whole apocalypse shtick for eons. Wyld and Weaver would create a universe, Wyrm would destroy it, they'd make a new one, Wyrm would destroy it again, and the cycle continued to repeat. And given how we have an entire group of Nephandi who are dedicated to serving the Wyrm (Malfeans), it would not be difficult to include them within that cycle.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for contradicting accounts, that's one of WoD's biggest failings in my opinion. The narrative is specifically presented in such a fashion that all the different splats exist within the same cosmology and are shouting over each other about how the world actually played out. Chronicles addressed this issue by having each of the different splats take place within their own self contained narratives, and only features cross overs if your ST decides to use them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>2</b> - Yes, but in this cosmological setting, humanity makes mistakes explicitly because it has been ordained by divine authority. It's not a product of humanity's own failings, it is God and his arch angels deliberately forcing them to choose the dark path. Which is why even a group that started with the best intentions, ultimately became corrupted. I don't want to live in the Imperium of Mankind, because the Imperium of Mankind is a fascist, totalitarian nightmare!<br /> <br /> Also, somebody made an entire video addressing that very Elden Ring quote. The video was explaining the <b>Lord of the Frenzied Flame's</b> point of view, by deconstructing the notion that life was precious, simply because it endured in the face of suffering. For every fortunate person out there who manages to rise above their suffering, there are those out there who fail to do so. Is it fair to them that their torment should continue for the sake of another's happiness?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>3</b> - You're far more helpless than you think. The existence of Paradox and Consensus prevents you from enacting any meaningful changes to reality, without introducing a dramatic shift in the global paradigm. But in order to do that, you're going to have to perform a mass culling of those who refuse to accept your world view. The early Traditionalists recognized this, and even proposed such an idea at one point.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, destroying reality is something that nearly all the Traditionalists are trying to accomplish as well, even if they don't recognize it at the moment.<br /> <br /> <br /> The paradigm that the Dreamspeakers wish to implement would lead to a world in which Wyld, Wyrm and Weaver are free to operate in the open for everyone to see. In a world where people accepted the existence of a Spirit World, you'd have Banes, Fomori, Drones and Gorgons running around all over the place. It would be the White Howlers vs the Roman Empire all over again.<br /> <br /> <br /> The paradigm of the Verbena harkens back to the days of ancient paganism, where we conducted ritualistic blood sacrifices. Imagine a Children of the Corn scenario, where your community has to crucify somebody every year to ensure a bountiful harvest? Or maybe you have to carve out somebody's heart every morning to make the sun rise?<br /> <br /> <br /> The paradigm of the Akashics would turn the world into a cultivation novel. Which sounds rad as hell at first, until your town is getting attacked by Yaoguais, and some wandering nomad slaughters an entire army by conjuring 1,000 flying swords on the battlefield.<br /> <br /> <br /> The paradigm of the Sons of Ether would create a world based on pseudo science. And while the idea of having rocket boots, laser pistols and steam powered mech suits is cool, this kind of paradigm would also support the existence of both racist and sexist ideologies.<br /> <br /> <br /> The paradigm of the Euthanatos would erase the fear of death, and not for the better I think. They would create a world in which people are seemingly detached from life. Euthanatoi refuse to let wraiths resolve their unfinished business, because allowing them to linger is disrupting the cycle of reincarnation. While the act of sanctified murdering those whom you feel have wasted their lives is seen as perfectly justifiable.<br /> <br /> I could probably go on, but this is getting a bit lengthy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-22T02:30:27-08:00","id":1557826,"title":"","content":"OK, rather than doing my own big response to all that... I gotta ask... where do you think you're going with all that? If you're trying to prove that the Nephandi have a point, it feels a lot more like you're missing what the books are saying about them than communicating that conclusion. The idea that you're conflating a potential cyclical nature to the WoD (something hinted at by the number of factions that believe in a wheel of ages cosmology, but not something ever demonstrated conclusively) with the idea that the Nephandi just want to end this instantiation of the universe doesn't really hold. The Nephandi aren't trying to reset the world and replace it with something better. They're trying to end it - including an potential new versions of it - and will settle for making it as worse as possible in the meantime; including making worse new instantiations if necessary.<br /> <br /> It also feels like you're grasping a lot. Not just from Mage, but from other game lines. You're pulling in things that seem far outside of their context or relevance to this discussion. For example while the WtA cosmology clearly puts the Triat in a cyclical nature, it never posits that it exists as part of a cosmic cycle of universal instantiations. They operate on a much more direct cyclical nature of creation, existence, and destruction that befits the WtA animist assumptions. The Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm operate solely on the universe they currently exist in with no known care for preexisting or potential future ones. That's no what they &quot;do&quot; as much as one can discuss the motives of such entities. <br /> <br /> This also holds true to equivocating about the idea of the Traditions wanting to &quot;end&quot; the world. There is a massive difference between wanting to change the world in a massive way, and wanting to cause the world to cease to exist and ensure it never comes into existence again. &quot;The end&quot; can be used in an imperfect sense where it signifies a transition rather than cessation (&quot;the end of an era&quot; does not mean that time itself has ended), or a perfect sense where in means the total lack of what previously was (&quot;death is the end of life&quot; means at least for an individual that there was a living organism and now there is dead matter as what made it alive is now ended). It doesn't help your points to swap between the two meanings.<br /> <br /> So again, where are you really trying to go with all this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-22T02:52:00-08:00","id":1557828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557826#post1557826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, rather than doing my own big response to all that... I gotta ask... where do you think you're going with all that? If you're trying to prove that the Nephandi have a point, it feels a lot more like you're missing what the books are saying about them than communicating that conclusion. The idea that you're conflating a potential cyclical nature to the WoD (something hinted at by the number of factions that believe in a wheel of ages cosmology, but not something ever demonstrated conclusively) with the idea that the Nephandi just want to end this instantiation of the universe doesn't really hold. The Nephandi aren't trying to reset the world and replace it with something better. They're trying to end it - including an potential new versions of it - and will settle for making it as worse as possible in the meantime; including making worse new instantiations if necessary.<br /> <br /> It also feels like you're grasping a lot. Not just from Mage, but from other game lines. You're pulling in things that seem far outside of their context or relevance to this discussion. For example while the WtA cosmology clearly puts the Triat in a cyclical nature, it never posits that it exists as part of a cosmic cycle of universal instantiations. They operate on a much more direct cyclical nature of creation, existence, and destruction that befits the WtA animist assumptions. The Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm operate solely on the universe they currently exist in with no known care for preexisting or potential future ones. That's no what they &quot;do&quot; as much as one can discuss the motives of such entities.<br /> <br /> This also holds true to equivocating about the idea of the Traditions wanting to &quot;end&quot; the world. There is a massive difference between wanting to change the world in a massive way, and wanting to cause the world to cease to exist and ensure it never comes into existence again. &quot;The end&quot; can be used in an imperfect sense where it signifies a transition rather than cessation (&quot;the end of an era&quot; does not mean that time itself has ended), or a perfect sense where in means the total lack of what previously was (&quot;death is the end of life&quot; means at least for an individual that there was a living organism and now there is dead matter as what made it alive is now ended). It doesn't help your points to swap between the two meanings.<br /> <br /> So again, where are you really trying to go with all this?</div> </div> </div> </div>My original point was to highlight the fact Nephandi are actually playable, due to how Ascension presents a free form sandbox style approach to magic. But at some point, we got sidetracked and it became a discussion about rationalizing their long term objective.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, I'm still reluctant to accept the idea that all Nephandi want to completely erase reality from existence, as that kind of makes the whole Exies faction redundant. Once again, the end times scenario definitely proves this is not the case, as the K'llsshaa end up taking over the world after the Outer Lords are brought into our reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even the Nephandi's own wikipedia page, and youtube videos states that a lot of them seek to reshape the world into something that is more appropriate in line with their own corrupted world view. Such a view may be anathema to humanity on a conceptual level, but that doesn't mean the universe is going to blip out of existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------<br /> <br /> One idea I see as being a potential inspiration comes from the games <i>'Lust for Darkness&quot;</i> and <i>&quot;Lust from Beyond'</i> It's a story about a cult of pleasure seekers who are trying to free an imprisoned god that caused its home universe to stagnate by making society so obsessed with indulging carnal pleasure, that they lost the ability to focus on anything else. Their every moment, every thought, every action is motivated solely by the overwhelming desire to engage in sexual debauchery.<br /> <br /> Society has collapsed, the very concept of self control has become alien to them, and the people have devolved into mindless sex addicts. Yet, despite its flaws, their god's universe continues to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-22T04:34:05-08:00","id":1557829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557828#post1557828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My original point was to highlight the fact Nephandi are actually playable, due to how Ascension presents a free form sandbox style approach to magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is contesting that the Nephandi have all the mechanics necessary in the system to be played. The question is are they functional characters to portray with the focus a PC gets compared to the abstractions NPCs allow the ST do to. Which makes the next bit inescapable:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But at some point, we got sidetracked and it became a discussion about rationalizing their long term objective. </div> </div> </div>Because this is Mage. Why a mage does what they do is integral and inseparable from how they do it. You keep proposing &quot;why&quot; answers that don't actually require a character to be a Nephandus, and frequently would play better as something else as it is. As has been said repeatedly, a character doesn't have to be a Nephandus to be evil. You don't even need to be a Mage that has made a pact with the darker forces of the WoD to be a Nephandus. What makes a character a Nephandus is that their Avatar has gone through the Cauls and come out different and twisted towards Descension. Which then gets to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I'm still reluctant to accept the idea that all Nephandi want to completely erase reality from existence, as that kind of makes the whole Exies faction redundant. </div> </div> </div>What a Nephandus wants is not inherently what drives their Avatar and Arete towards it's fully potential. Lots of Nephandi think they can go into the Cauls for the power, and think that they can stop once the world is to their liking. They can't. The Cauls ensure they'll go farther despite their desires. Even something like letting the Outer Lords in, is only a stepping stone to the end result of complete annihilation of reality. Eventually their Avatars will want more than the hellscapes lesser evils can provide, and eventually said Avatars will get what they want if the Nephandi aren't stopped; even if the Avatar decides their current Mage isn't good enough and decides to help that one die so they can get a new one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Society has collapsed, the very concept of self control has become alien to them, and the people have devolved into mindless sex addicts. Yet, despite its flaws, their god's universe continues to exist. </div> </div> </div>And what makes this a scenario that's specific to the Nephandi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-22T06:51:23-08:00","id":1557831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557828#post1557828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I'm still reluctant to accept the idea that all Nephandi want to completely erase reality from existence, as that kind of makes the whole Exies faction redundant. Once again, the end times scenario definitely proves this is not the case, as the K'llsshaa end up taking over the world after the Outer Lords are brought into our reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>So here's the thing. We have actual indications of what happens when a Nephandus doesn't necessarily want to destroy the world or even to be evil, because that's the state the Widderslainte start out in. Whatever their starting goals are they are driven to be Nephandi by their Avatars. Some fight it, some don't, but the indication is all of them fall. So I can agree with you that many Nephandi might not currently want to erase all reality, but unless they somehow manage to resist their Avatar, that doesn't matter. And based on track records, they can't do that forever.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-22T09:21:30-08:00","id":1557834,"title":"","content":"We clearly have severe ontological differences in how to approach the material. Instead of looking to the game in order to perceive the core message, themes and moods that it's trying to convey, there's these... &quot;appeals to lore&quot;, that are at best out of context and, at worst, disingenuous. Instead of taking the discussion to the themes that are <i>explicitly in the books</i>, there's these &quot;gotcha/ummm actually&quot; answers that ignore core fundamentals of the books, as if the writers themselves can't grasp their own work. <i>It's there: Hope and Transformation; Defiance and Reflection</i>. On the very pages I cited (and that I won't cite anymore, for the risk that I will become a parody of myself), but actually Consensus and Paradox are these gargatuan forces that impede player agency. <i>So why play at all</i><i>? </i>The use of paradigm &quot;The paradigm of the Dreamspeaker/Sons of Ether/etc.&quot; as if there is a notion of a unified paradigm throughout the factions, ignoring the indiosyncrasies of belief portrayed in Mage and how paradigm, as a mechanic, interacts with other aspects of the setting, like focus and instruments. Even the apocryphal nature of WoD, it's there <i>by desing</i>, so that Storytellers can decide which version of the metaplot (if at all) they are gonna use in their own stories. WoD, and specially Mage, is composed of works that are not static in their presentation, like a mediocre Marvel movie or some such, in which there's nothing to it except what's given in a silver plater. It's not a book or a movie in which the work just passively asserts itself to the viewer, but a game that dares you to interact with what's trying to say about so many complex themes, with each argument in order to &quot;prove the writers wrong&quot; just diminishing the work to one more besides all other grimdark-ish settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28986-agrat","name":"Agrat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28986_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T04:30:10-08:00","id":1557852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557829#post1557829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what makes this a scenario that's specific to the Nephandi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the imprisoned god's universe has come to a screeching halt. I wasn't speaking hyperbole when I said their every action is motivated by the desire to seek pleasure. They literally can not focus on anything else.<br /> <br /> Society no longer exists, civilization has collapsed. Their cities and monuments are left to decay, while the denizens of this ruined universe shamble around in a mindless stupor, looking for something to fuck.<br /> <br /> The cultists have made contact with this universe, and are trying to find a way to free the imprisoned god, so they can bring him to earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T05:37:21-08:00","id":1557854,"title":"","content":"Well, that sounds a lot like Voormas endgame. Except instead of ending death, it's eternal bliss gone wrong<br /> <br /> It's my understanding that Nephandi would oppose such an universe on principle. Tho this one isn't quite AS bad for Nephandi, as it could make Nephandic endgame easier<br /> <br /> Hell on Earth types could seek to corrupt or twist the god so instead of pleasure and stupor, people would experience only pain and suffering. End Everything types could be ok with the fact this god eradicated society, but would eventually try to ascelerate decay as it seems obliteration it's taking way too long.<br /> <br /> Both could articulate this desire as something noble, as the status quo it's certainly not great. They could temporarily ally with other mages to do this. But ultimate their desire it's not going to end well for anyone, not even in this scenario - they don't want the wheel to keep spinning and people to be free, they want to clog it, to derail it even more than it already is.<br /> <br /> This is one cool scenario to have a Nephandus NPC helping the PCs that want to free the god - only to betray them at the end as their true goal wasn't to free the god but to corrupt it. I would still not allow a Nephandus PC unless everyone it's on board with this (including me), understanding that this IS going to end in betrayal and/or horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":".  gramatical errors 01-23-2026, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T06:31:00-08:00","id":1557855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557854#post1557854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both could articulate this desire as something noble, as the status quo it's certainly not great. They could temporarily ally with other mages to do this. But ultimate their desire it's not going to end well for anyone, not even in this scenario - they don't want the wheel to keep spinning and people to be free, they want to clog it, to derail it even more than it already is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's kind of what ends up happening at the end of the second game. Like any good Lovecraftian horror, the very existence of such a being has a mind warping affect on all who witnesses it. People start going insane with lust, and the guy who was acting as leader of the cult suddenly gets the overwhelming urge to use the corpse of a woman he was about to bury to relieve himself.<br /> <br /> <br /> If my memory serves me correctly, those affected by the imprisoned god's influence even lose the ability to feel pain. As even getting her face blasted off with a shotgun is treated like a minor inconvenience for one of the cultists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T12:32:17-08:00","id":1557863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557852#post1557852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The cultists have made contact with this universe, and are trying to find a way to free the imprisoned god, so they can bring him to earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but they're the antagonists of the game. If you were running a Mage game inspired by those video games... the Nephandi would be the bad guy NPCs, not the PCs. The characters you play in the games are trying to stop the cultists from bringing that entity into the human world.<br /> <br /> If anything the example just demonstrates why people are generally on board with not having playable Nephandi:<br /> <br /> 1) You'd be stuck playing a character actively prioritizing shallow immediate pleasure over all else; even if it requires depraved violence to achieve<br /> <br /> 2) PvP would definitely be an issue as the imprisoned demiurge's human followers tend to treat opposing views on how to do things with violence, and any non-Nephandi PCs would be targets for sexual violence in order to corrupt them.<br /> <br /> 3) The few antagonists that seem to legitimately regret how far they've gone either rationalize continuing on their path anyway, or kill themselves as the only way to stop (or at least get themselves killed on purpose). Only reinforcing that becoming a Nephandus is a line you can't uncross even if what you're being pushed to do by other forces starts going past whatever goals you had in the first place.<br /> <br /> This seems a fairly straightforward example on pretty much every front of why not to play Nephandi as PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T23:12:39-08:00","id":1557872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557863#post1557863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1) You'd be stuck playing a character actively prioritizing shallow immediate pleasure over all else; even if it requires depraved violence to achieve</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I like playing my characters. The Unga Bunga approach to problem solving never fails to be cathartic. I'd let my characters go HAM a lot more often, if the splats didn't have a suppressor built into their gameplay mechanics (Humanity, Paradox, Bedlam, est).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat:</b> <i>&quot;Pretending that you're still human is fucking cringe. Here, take a look at these brochures and see if any of the Paths resonate with you.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Court:</b> <i>&quot;Dreams may fade, but trauma lingers. If you can't inspire hope anymore, why not instill them with fear?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ratkin:</b> <i>&quot;Don't you dare say I'm too extreme, when you've got four different tribes of Garou advocating for some form of global genocide!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-23T23:53:19-08:00","id":1557873,"title":"","content":"Then the Nephandi aren't really your speed regardless. High aggro evil mages are used by true Nephandi as pawns and their deaths help convince the other factions the Nephandi are being contained. If you want to &quot;go ham&quot; in Mage, a faction that values being sneaky subtle manipulators isn't really the right fit; morals be damned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-24T04:15:17-08:00","id":1557874,"title":"","content":"I was lead to believe the Nephandi are winning the Ascension war, and have infiltrated pretty much every available group. I've seen it stated multiple times over the years.<br /> <br /> Also, did I miss something, or did you just contradict yourself? You told me playing a Nephandi would have to be a psychotic murder hobo, but now you're telling me those kind of Nephandi are basically the group's version of Shovelheads?<br /> <br /> Which implies that it actually is possible for the Nephandi to pose as functional members of society. You can't infiltrate another organization, if you're going around flipping the switch and shouting <i>&quot;chaos take the world!&quot;</i> at random intervals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-24T15:05:12-08:00","id":1557884,"title":"","content":"I can't really help you with what you were somehow lead to believe. I can do my best to relate what's in the books as I understand them.<br /> <br /> How well the Nehpandi are doing is up to the ST. Though it is worth noting that successfully having infiltrators in the Traditions and the Technocracy isn't the same as winning... Mage is an intrigue heavy game and both of those factions are constantly trying to spy on each other too. Their success rates with the smaller Crafts/Disparates is considerably lower because there just aren't that many mages to go around for the Nephandi to have agents in all of those groups. The Disparates especially contain some of the best Nephandi hunters in the setting (and the Disparate Alliance is founded specifically on recognizing that the Nephandi are a bigger threat than the Tradtions or Union are taking them as).<br /> <br /> And I don't see myself I having stated a contradiction. As I see it you're conflating my statement about a specific example (translating the video games you mentioned) and then treating it overly broadly to the Nephandi as a whole. Nephandi modeled after the cults in those games are going to be extremely hyperfocused because they serve a hyperfocused entity. I never said murderhobo or psychotic. And I stated back in the 8th post of the thread that the Nephandi operate on a two-tier system where members that aren't capable of the subtly necessary to survive every other group of mages wanting them dead (and a good deal of other Nephandi seeking to backstab them) aren't treated as &quot;true&quot; Nephandi but as disposable pawns. That's nothing new in my position. Shovelheads isn't really an appropriate comparison because making a shovehead is relatively low investment. Mages are rare and can't be &quot;made&quot; like vampires. The Sabbat also have a two-tier system where they consider &quot;vampire&quot; and &quot;Cainite&quot; different categories. Only vampires that have proven themselves loyal to the Sabbat cause earn the status as &quot;true&quot; Cainites with the freedoms and rights in the Sabbat codes that implies.<br /> <br /> And yes, I'm not sure why you'd be surprised by the idea of Nephandi that can pose as functional members of society... those are the ones that use the unga bunga ones as pawns to help maintain that facade. The ones going ham are crappy infiltrators and thus seen as the lowest and most disposable mages associated with the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-24T17:49:39-08:00","id":1557885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557884#post1557884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How well the Nehpandi are doing is up to the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple choice scenario!<br /> <br /> On one hand, I kind of like that we have different options to go with in regards to how the metaplot operates.<br /> <br /> But on the other, it kind of makes any discussions regarding the metaplot impossible. Since anybody can just chime in with a counter take on the situation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 01-24-2026, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-24T18:55:23-08:00","id":1557886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557885#post1557885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on the other, it kind of makes any discussions regarding the metaplot impossible. Since anybody can just chime in with a counter take on the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's totally irrelevant, tho. How well the Nephandi are doing doesn't translate to them being playable or not.<br /> <br /> Mage has never cared much about that, you can join a House of Hermes that has *two* members (making you the 3rd most powerful mage of the House <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). You can join Crafts that are nearly extint, if Crafts are allowed. Or play with as part of the migthy Technocracy.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, playing a Technocrat out of a Technocracy game, when most players are Traditionalists - is going to be much more polemical in spite of them being fully endorsed as playable.<br /> <br /> The conundrums of playing a Nephandi aren't related to their success, but to how they are portrayed as this almost certain betrayal bunch that are hardcoded as &quot;evil for evil sake&quot; with very little agency on their part to change it.<br /> <br /> Yeah, they're superb infiltrators. Their favorite tactic it's to throw other Nephandi under the bus, so nobody can suspect of their rigtheousness. Their goal it's to bring ruin to whatever structure they're infiltrating, corrupting as many mages as they can.<br /> <br /> It's very hard to see how to make a functional group out of this, not because they can be succesful but because that success it's paved on the bodies of their mates. And their whole hierarchy functions like this - you're on top until the ones below you can get you down.<br /> <br /> Maybe there's a story out there for them as PC, but nothing here on this thread really shines as an example I would want to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-24T20:29:25-08:00","id":1557887,"title":"","content":"Kinda? While M20 leaves this as variable, it does detail the main options and we can discuss each in turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-25T16:41:36-08:00","id":1557905,"title":"","content":"My problem with the idea of playing a Nephandus is that they lack free will by definition. For example, the nephandi can't just choose not to be cruel. They have to be focused on the greater evil. I find that to restrictive. <br /> <br /> Yes, I've played characters bound by vows. But it is a choice to keep a vow. Nephandi don't get choices. There's a group of evil mages in <b>Dragons of the East</b> who are being compelled to do evil. The struggle of these mages to fight against the evil they are trapped in is dramatic. The Nephandi by definition can't struggle anymore. The cannibal mages can still make free will choices to restrict their evil acts. A Nephandus can't even form the thought to want to reject evil.<br /> <br /> What a bore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-25T19:29:40-08:00","id":1557908,"title":"","content":"I think the &quot;complete lack of free will&quot; argument goes a bit far. Nephandi might not get an ultimate say in where their Avatars will push them, but their Avatars do have to push. The books have presented Nephandi that have realized they made a bad deal after the fact even if they don't see a way out. Nephandi are also usually free enough to act with longer term evil in mind. They can bide their time for years, even decades in order to execute their plans. They don't have to stop and kick a puppy just because it's there there are bigger goals at hand for them to be concerned with. It's the Nephandi without dedication to bigger goals that usually end up indulging in capricious cruelty.<br /> <br /> That, to me at least, means there is some will in them (they're still mages after all), even if their fate's are sealed to the point where even an archmaster of Entropy and expert in Nephandi Avatar reincarnation is still in the experimental phase of possibly having a cure for undoing that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T04:35:59-08:00","id":1557911,"title":"","content":"Agreed, they don't have freedom to chose their path. They're constantly driven to do evil, and have to cave in in order to grow. But there's a lot of ways to interpret that inverted path.<br /> <br /> That's how you have Nephandi that want to get rich and powerful.<br /> <br /> The difference with other villans it's that an egoist craving of wanting to get rich and powerful isn't sufficent reason of their cruelty.<br /> <br /> One could argue that such desires it's what makes them &quot;more human&quot;, even, providing a framework that could push them to *not* kick the dog if only because it isn't convinient - all the while their spirits pushes them to achieve those all too human goals in the most evil ways possible.<br /> <br /> As I see it, you sort of have to *invert* the typical villan stereotype. Rather than having all too human reasons to be evil, they are evil yet have use of reason as any human and can express that evil in different ways (and even try to figth it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-26-2026, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T17:49:22-08:00","id":1557934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557908#post1557908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the &quot;complete lack of free will&quot; argument goes a bit far.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The Nephandi were not tricked into the service of evil. They actively chose to enter it.<br /> <br /> In order to survive passage through the Caul, the Nephandus must freely and wholeheartedly pledge themselves in service to everything they see as evil and fucked up in the world.<br /> <br /> They deliberately want to be this way. If they did not, then their experience in the Caul would have killed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T20:30:55-08:00","id":1557936,"title":"","content":"The Nephandi can absolutely be tricked into the service of evil. A character has to enter the Cauls of their own free will, but nothing stops a recruiting Nephandi from using all sorts of deception to get that to happen; unsurprisingly the Nephandi aren't dedicated to fully informed consent. It's entirely unknown if someone tricked into the Caul without a desire to pledge themselves to evil can survive the process. Why some that go in die is left mysterious; even those completely dedicated to evil before hand don't always survive the process. Since the books never define how exactly the Cauls work, we don't know what a mage has to do to come out alive; we just know that any that do survive get their Avatar's inverted. It's even possible some mages go in and simply disappear to somewhere else at the whims of whatever dark forces power the Cauls in the first place. <br /> <br /> Since those that go in and make it back out all end up on the path to Descension regardless, it's largely academic though. Once they willing took that step in, they stuck with that choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T13:12:38-07:00","id":1562271,"title":"","content":"Just to address one point I saw rereading the thread: Nefandi are not Mages. Not in the ontological sense.<br /> <br /> This is important because their powers don't follow three fundamental rules:<br /> <br /> 1. Doesn't come from their own Will;<br /> <br /> 2. Doesn't require Paradigm; and<br /> <br /> 3. Don't leave &quot;normal&quot; Resonance.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Doesn't come from their own Will</b></u>:<br /> <br /> Nefandi are channeling erasure. Their magic is innately destructive, even when it appears to generate a creative effect.<br /> <br /> Every single effect a Nefandus produces is unraveling reality regardless of their goals, their will being a tool for Oblivion rather than the other way around.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Doesn't require Paradigm</b></u>:<br /> <br /> This is important and not a small thing. They choose Instruments out of convenience or habit, not of belief. Some may believe the need, but they don't, actually.<br /> <br /> As long as their powers destroy reality (with or without their knowledge), anything goes.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Don't leave &quot;normal&quot; Resonance</b></u>:<br /> <br /> Resonance usually reacts to a lot of factors. It depends on the Mage, the area, the spell, the goal, the Quintessence/Tass used and so on. It is a poorly written, vague rule, but still central to the game, because Resonance codifies the relationship between Magic and the world, its effects on the Mage and its interactions with other things that carry Resonance.<br /> <br /> Nefandi only leave Nefandic Resonance, which may be treated as a singular signature or small family of them, but ignores all factors anyway. It's stronger than normal, unique to them and unavoidable for them. The game sometimes presents means for them to &quot;cover&quot; this, but not to not leave it there. This is the mark of the unraveling they promote, and as any Resonance can have further effects if the ST so chooses.<br /> <br /> One must be a Mage to become Barabi, but the result is not a Mage, even if it is something superficially similar that uses the same rules for ease of play (that's also stated). Whatever they Inverted Avatar is, it effectively turned the character into something else that's a servant to Dark Magic rather than a user.<br /> <br /> But that said, I agree &quot;no free will&quot; is a bit of an overstatement. They have some agency, limited as it may be. Unraveling the universe isn't a plan or goal for them, it is fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T14:45:32-07:00","id":1562279,"title":"","content":"I don't see how that makes an argument that they're not mages in an ontological sense (or any other).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure of any book that states that metaphysically having an inverted Avatar changes the Nephandus's need to will their effects into existence. They might have access to other powers, but so do normal mages.<br /> <br /> There's nothing that says they don't have to contend with having a Focus just like any other mage; which means they have Paradigms. What's the evidence that their Instruments are fundamentally different from, say, an Orphan where they might come more from circumstance and convenience rather than training? All mages are theoretically capable of overcoming their Focus. It's the Technocrats, not the Nephandi, that are stated as having the most difficulty with this. All non-Technocrats can spend WP and take increased difficulty for &quot;anything goes.<br /> <br /> Having a unique Resonance follows from having an altered Avatar... by itself this doesn't really create some category error with considering them mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T07:12:44-07:00","id":1562301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1562271#post1562271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u><b>Doesn't require Paradigm</b></u>:<br /> <br /> This is important and not a small thing. They choose Instruments out of convenience or habit, not of belief. Some may believe the need, but they don't, actually.<br /> <br /> As long as their powers destroy reality (with or without their knowledge), anything goes.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Clarification needed:</b> but doesn't one theory state that the <i>'Qlipothic Spheres'</i> are drawing power from previous universes that the Nephandi already destroyed?<br /> <br /> Which is to say that the reason why they appear able to skirt the rules of magic, is because their magic comes from a totally separate reality, where the laws are different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T08:49:13-07:00","id":1562306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1562301#post1562301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Clarification needed:</b> but doesn't one theory state that the <i>'Qlipothic Spheres'</i> are drawing power from previous universes that the Nephandi already destroyed?<br /> <br /> Which is to say that the reason why they appear able to skirt the rules of magic, is because their magic comes from a totally separate reality, where the laws are different?</div> </div> </div> </div>Many theories say many things. There's not a single person who actually knows what they truly are besides the following:<br /> <br /> 1. Nefandi can only access Qlippothic Spheres. The reverse isn't true.<br /> <br /> 2. The actual rules for them were deliberately omitted, the regular Spheres are a placeholder.<br /> <br /> 3. During the Caul, they journey through their Shard Realms. There's no other known way to reach those Realms, for anyone.<br /> <br /> 4. Qlippothic Shard Realms are somewhat well described so anyone who wants to extrapolate is free to do so, though the devs won't.<br /> <br /> 5. Regular Mages using Qlippothic Spheres are not subject to any deleterious effect or enticed to do evil. They're just Spheres.<br /> <br /> And that's it. Until further notice those are just Spheres with their Shard Realms. Everything beyond that is purely speculation. And bringing different laws to reality is already what every Mage does, especially with Spirit.<br /> <br /> Nefandi Magic is primarily stated as anathema to reality, but the precise reason and relation to their Shard Realms is unknown. Is their Magic drawing from other realities? Siphoning our reality elsewhere? Colliding both realities for an annihilation like matter vs antimatter? It may even be unrelated, their Magic is anathema to our reality AND linked to Qlippothic Spheres as independent effects.<br /> <br /> I stand corrected by Heavy Arms, though, that affirming Nefandi aren't Mages is a bit too far. But I'll still defend they don't follow a regular Paradigm. Their descriptions frequently imply far more freedom in how to do Magic, with the choice of Instruments becoming personal taste. I'm without my books at the moment to confirm, though.<br /> <br /> What I don't know is how much the game stirs close or away from the actual Qlippoth from Kabbalah, which could or not elucidate more or the matter. I'm neither knowledgeable in this area or in a position to speculate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T10:19:51-07:00","id":1562308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1562306#post1562306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything beyond that is purely speculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Great Horned Rat</a> is referencing the sidebar on page 204 of <i>Ascension</i>. Not so much a 'theory' as a piece of setting building for a specific type of game world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I don't know is how much the game stirs close or away from the actual Qlippoth from Kabbalah, which could or not elucidate more or the matter. I'm neither knowledgeable in this area or in a position to speculate. </div> </div> </div>Not very. I think it's pulling from the imagery of modern occultism which is downstream of Christian cabbalah, which in turn is downstream of Jewish Kabbalah; keeping in mind that at each new stage the people adapting it to their system didn't necessarily understand it that well (or frankly were not interested in doing so).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-06T07:25:59-07:00","id":1563869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agrat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1557821#post1557821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a dialogue from Melina in Elden Ring: &quot;<i>However ruined this world has become, however mired in torment and despair. Life endures. Births continue. There is beauty in that, is there not?&quot;</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know this is a necro post, but I thought up a rebuttal to this quote, and I had to share it.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;There are microbes living in a pile of shit. But that doesn't make a turd any more appealing, now does it? &quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-08T13:31:10-07:00","id":1563921,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's a good rebutal. Life being beautiful doesn't imply nor require all life-forms to be beautiful at all times.<br /> <br /> So you being grossed out by turds doesn't count as a rebutal...If anything, it's the <i>opposite</i>, we're back where we started: The quote it's telling you that turds are gross but they're part of the cycle of life, and making them gone tis' going to do all kinds of bad to the parts of life you <i>do</i> like.<br /> <br /> BUT...it left me with a reflection I wanted to share: <hr /><br /> Turds are unpleasant to us because we are human. Flies don't reject the animal turd like we do. It's tied to our biology, maybe to our survival (I'm no expert evolutionist, tho) - yet on this context the arguments it's being said to justify a position <i>antithetical</i> to all of this.<br /> <br /> Nephandi complain all day about how &quot;the world it's shit&quot;, yet in practice they want to make an even bigger turd: They would create a world antithetical to human life as we know it either as end goal, or as a step to reach their end goal. There's no description of the odour of the &quot;Hell on Earth&quot;, but it doesn't seem like it would be what we would normaly consider <i>pleasing </i><br /> <br /> That makes me think that, other than Nephandi being just hipocrites about all of this (very likely), this could be a good example of how their mindset it's being twisted by an <i>alien thing</i> that has a different perspective about the world:<br /> <br /> Nephandi complain that the world it's shit, but the shit parts we would normaly complain about aren't the <i>problem.</i> If anything their actions prove they want more suffering, ruin and decay. Maybe to <i>end it all at once</i>, true, but certainly they don't seem to have a problem <i>specificly with the shit</i>. For the thing that infects their soul, either there's no difference between turds and roses or the turd actually smells better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-08-2026, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-08T21:30:25-07:00","id":1563927,"title":"","content":"Even the idea that it's to end it all at once is false, as they don't seem to be hasty about it or anything.<br /> <br /> Whatever a Nefandus thinks they're working towards, what they're really doing is aimless suffering for the sake of it. Slowly building up, with no concern for any structured plan or goal.<br /> <br /> One important aspect of their actions: success is not the point. They're not efficient. They're not abated by setbacks. They don't care when big disasters are averted. They're definitely not giving a damn if degradation is fast or not. As long as the result has more overall suffering in the world in absolutely any sense, they're happy.<br /> <br /> Making the world worse is the only measure of success that matters to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-09T07:12:18-07:00","id":1563932,"title":"","content":"Part of the gimmick of the Nephandi is that as a group they have extremely hazy and open ended win conditions. It's very easy to seem like the most effective faction and rack up victory after victory when you can count anything as a victory. &quot;Okay, so I didn't say the words exactly right, so the summoning failed and Chattur'gha won't be consuming the world and reigning for 1,000 years of terror, but hey, I made over a hundred people up to five minutes late for work, so... Victory for Me!&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, there's a little bit of hyperbole there, but mostly just in making the hypothetical Nephandus look inept. I could easily imagine a more capable one putting a much better spin on spreading low level suffering to hundreds or thousands of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-09T11:19:01-07:00","id":1563937,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much it.<br /> <br /> As long as they can spin it in any way where their actions made someone's life suck more, it's a win. As a trope they are designed to be an easy &quot;invincible faction&quot; you can ascribe victory to almost regardless of what actually happens.<br /> <br /> But for a character the problem is that it makes for a faction where your actions matter little. It doesn't matter if you win because everything is a win, your achievements are of little relevance since it capitalized on your results whatever they are, even becoming internally powerful is of little relevance because no member matters.<br /> <br /> Playing a Nefandus is playing someone whose personal stakes don't matter to a story, if they exist at all. Your personal win conditions have no meaning to the faction one way or another. Your survival fundamentally doesn't matter. It isn't irrelevant in the sense that it is acceptable as sacrifice, but that literally it won't change the group in any way.<br /> <br /> You'd be just one more in the endless parade of performative jerks whose point in existing is to cause any discomfort at all. Even if you think you have more autonomy or whatever, it is not something you have as a Nefandus but despite of it, and being a Nefandus makes it pointless, you're part of a machine of formless, aimless, thoughtless evil.<br /> <br /> Crucially, in a game centered around belief, the Nefandus make beliefs pointless. They are not propagating an ideology, or a coherent vision of the world. They just seek suffering, and what a member believes is inconsequential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-09T12:34:39-07:00","id":1563939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563937#post1563937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crucially, in a game centered around belief, the Nefandus make beliefs pointless. They are not propagating an ideology, or a coherent vision of the world. They just seek suffering, and what a member believes is inconsequential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the point of the OP wasn't to argue that they have any cause to fight for, or paradigm to rally around. It was to highlight the fact they are still playable, despite the book making every attempt to emphasize that they don't want them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-09T21:01:50-07:00","id":1563947,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, I think it's as much about setting expectations for what a Storytelling game is &quot;meant&quot; to be as anything else.<br /> WoD began, at least in part, as a direct rebellion against the fantasy RPGs of the time that were more freeform board games than role-playing. Game rules as a lose facilitator for stories of personal exploration. Dark and edgy and punk, but also processing anxiety and trauma, exploring identity and boundaries in the safety of fiction.<br /> <br /> In that context, playing the role of a Nephandus is categorically unhealthy. Dark characters? Manipulative characters? Even outright evil characters? All in-bounds. Even the nastiest Tzimisce or Baali is a tool for exploring personal horror.<br /> <br /> But Nephandi really are meant to be something else. Mage's is the horror of being in a world too small for your ambitions. If you don't see why getting into the headspace of an ontological nihilist whose greatest ambition is manipulating <i>all other people</i> into hopelessness and self-destruction is a different level of darkness from a villain &quot;just&quot; trying to destroy the world or murder people or whatever... I envy you.<br /> <br /> Which is all to say, if you *don't* want to play Mage as that type of self-reflective game, that's fine! But I can't fault designers who intended to create a certain experience for not supporting the idea of playing a character that, if also represented as intended, would not be okay to experience that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 09-10-2026, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T06:06:25-07:00","id":1563952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563937#post1563937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd be just one more in the endless parade of performative jerks whose point in existing is to cause any discomfort at all. Even if you think you have more autonomy or whatever, it is not something you have as a Nefandus but despite of it, and being a Nefandus makes it pointless, you're part of a machine of formless, aimless, thoughtless evil.<br /> <br /> Crucially, in a game centered around belief, the Nefandus make beliefs pointless. They are not propagating an ideology, or a coherent vision of the world. They just seek suffering, and what a member believes is inconsequential.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no textual evidence of this, but at least to me it seems like Nephandi were written as a deliberate response to a certain type of performative nihilism and abuse that was so trendy in goth circles in the 90s. Like, if you took that affect seriously as a philosophy (and empowered it the way that only Mage can reify a philosophy) you don't get cool subversive villains, you get unplayable monsters. Because this is fundamentally a game about the Creative Urge, and that affect *has nothing creative to say* and so in Mage can't even *have a real Avatar* let alone use real spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T11:05:53-07:00","id":1563954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563937#post1563937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's pretty much it.<br /> Even if you think you have more autonomy or whatever, it is not something you have as a Nefandus but despite of it, and being a Nefandus makes it pointless, you're part of a machine of formless, aimless, thoughtless evil.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;Tell me, is it slavery when you get what you want?&quot;</i> - Majin Vegeta<br /> <br /> Since everyone on these forums keeps telling me the Nephandi are driven by an urge for universal destruction, despite the fact nearly all of their factions are actively striving for something else, let's use that as a rationalization for the whole autonomy aspect.<br /> <br /> To a Nephandus who is seeking to destroy the universe, selling their soul to a demon lord is simply a means to an end. The consequences of such a choice are ultimately irrelevant, since there won't be a Hell, once they reduce everything back to the cosmic void from whence it came.<br /> <br /> The Nephandus can traffic with demons, and engage in all manner of horrific atrocities, without fear of reprisal, because there won't be anyone left to reprise them when all is said and done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T13:34:22-07:00","id":1563957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563939#post1563939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the point of the OP wasn't to argue that they have any cause to fight for, or paradigm to rally around. It was to highlight the fact they are still playable, despite the book making every attempt to emphasize that they don't want them to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which wasn't argued by anyone, not even by the book. You've been already repeatedly told that, the OP is wrong because it misses the actual point, not 'cause anyone thinks playing a Nefandus is mechanically unsupported in any way, or even hard to do.<br /> <br /> The argument is why playing one is a bad idea. The book refuses to give them the full faction treatment because playing them is a bad idea. That's all there is to it.<br /> <br /> So my comment, and those of everyone since the first responses to your OP 5 pages ago, is in the sense that playing a Nefandus isn't that secret cheat code the devs don't want you to find. It is just plain stupid, and if you don't see it it's more probable that you misunderstood the faction, and what you can do at other factions.<br /> <br /> Because if there's one thing that mages can be with almost no push back, in any faction in the game, is absolutely monstrous.<br /> <br /> Nefandi don't add to this evil, they just remove other elements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563947#post1563947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WoD began, at least in part, as a direct rebellion against the fantasy RPGs of the time that were more freeform board games than role-playing. Game rules as a lose facilitator for stories of personal exploration. Dark and edgy and punk, but also processing anxiety and trauma, exploring identity and boundaries in the safety of fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with most you said, and there were many fans and some authors of WoD that believed this rationale, I must remind all that this is utterly bullshit.<br /> <br /> RPGs of the time, and from decades before, had plenty of distinctive roleplay experiences to offer, different takes on rules to facilitate personal exploration, and proposals to explore identity and boundaries and many other things.<br /> <br /> A big part of what made WoD fit the particular niche that made it prosper was to actually use a system that was thoroughly simulationist, the most traditional one could get. It was arguably the alternative to classic D&amp;D design that most resembled classic D&amp;D design at a time even D&amp;D sought to present wildly different design approaches.<br /> <br /> I've read &quot;demonstrations&quot; of the time of how WoD had a roleplay focused system that work different, and 19 out of 20 of those were just pathetic excuses to bad design where blatant errors were presented as secretly good things if you just apply the Golden Rule or punish players that &quot;play wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> Most people who praise WoD as a superior RP experience, even for the time, never tried other games or tried Forgotten Realms in bad faith, because the assumption never held any water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563952#post1563952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no textual evidence of this, but at least to me it seems like Nephandi were written as a deliberate response to a certain type of performative nihilism and abuse that was so trendy in goth circles in the 90s. Like, if you took that affect seriously as a philosophy (and empowered it the way that only Mage can reify a philosophy) you don't get cool subversive villains, you get unplayable monsters. Because this is fundamentally a game about the Creative Urge, and that affect *has nothing creative to say* and so in Mage can't even *have a real Avatar* let alone use real spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all over the place in the WoD and is a result of the Punk philosophy that is the thread linking all lines (no, the thread isn't Gothic).<br /> <br /> It's hard for some to understand because the performative aesthetics of Punk is nihilistic to a fault, but that's precisely why Punks have so much aversion to Posers: it's not that Punks just don't like imitators like everyone else, but rather this imitation is inherently antithetical to the Philosophy, not just empty.<br /> <br /> Punk philosophy has a nonnegotiable tenet of fighting the good fight. The world is horrible, but it is not lost. Anger is valuable if it makes you hold your ground against exploitation. The fight will be long and arduous, and for most of it the only reward will be satisfaction of doing it, so it needs passion, but it can bring a better future.<br /> <br /> Every &quot;valid&quot; faction gives us a vision of what a better future is, and even futures that look bad for most are legitimated by a faction that can still paint it as better.<br /> <br /> Nefandi, the Wyrm, standard Baali, Specters, those factions are antagonists because they just embrace nihilism: nothing matters and we won't actually try to build something better. We don't even believe the status quo is valid, we'll just shit on everything until the world become its worse version for everyone, we included.<br /> <br /> And this is what a fucking Poser looks like and any Punk worth their salt know Posers deserve no rest or mercy, the pathetic assholes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563954#post1563954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;Tell me, is it slavery when you get what you want?&quot;</i> - Majin Vegeta</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Yes, it is.<br /> <br /> Majin Vegeta is an idiot and Vegeta admits it.<br /> <br /> Also, the Nefandi aren't outsmarting anyone, the whole point is that they'll get to live in the same misery as everyone else. Their overall goal has roughly three phases:<br /> <br /> Phase 1: deteriorate the universe. This is a long term situation during which your masters won't shield you from consequences, the opposite, your masters and colleagues will give you an even worse time than regular consequences could, which is one of the reasons you don't care about them.<br /> <br /> Phase 2: the last twitches of the dying universe that also take an undefined and potentially incommensurately long time. Everything is hell for everyone, so now everyone get to experience your standard living conditions from Phase 1. You're a part of everyone.<br /> <br /> Phase 3: the universe dies. Either nothing else exists anymore or what comes after is totally unknown. You can dream that this is the ticket to become a god, but this is basically wishful thinking, real evidence doesn't give anything, or point to things not getting better for you.<br /> <br /> Observation: any theory where you end up as a creator god if your own universe must be balanced against the fact that you'll do so only after being exposed to constant suffering to an absolutely unhealthy point, so it's possible that your godlike self will be too deranged and emotionally pathetic to be able to create anything that actually improves their lot.<br /> <br /> But that's it. You've been told all of this and more several times, you've been shown that the character concepts you associate with Nefandi aren't actually related to them, and you've been repeatedly told that you can play the character you want, as horrific as you want, Nefandus or not, just go ahead and do it.<br /> <br /> Why are you still trying to convince players with sometimes decades of experience that they are wrong about everything they actually know about the game, when they're not even saying you can't do what you want to do?<br /> <br /> Just do it already, dammit! Actual experience playing a Nefandus, while it won't change those opinions magically, will add actual interesting arguments and observations in lieu of repeating inane shallow interpretations without any new twist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T13:34:23-07:00","id":1563958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563954#post1563954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;Tell me, is it slavery when you get what you want?&quot;</i> - Majin Vegeta</div> </div> </div> </div>The sacrifice afterwards seems so point that he wanted other things, but was just being stubborn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since everyone on these forums keeps telling me the Nephandi are driven by an urge for universal destruction, despite the fact nearly all of their factions are actively striving for something else, let's use that as a rationalization for the whole autonomy aspect. </div> </div> </div>This is pointless because nobody said that Nephandi can't strive for something else. What most of us are trying to say it's those other goals have nothing *Nephandic* on them. A Nephandus doesn't have those goals because they're Nephandi, but because they're -still- a person.<br /> <br /> Nephandi are driven by an urge for universal destruction (or horror, or both) trough their Avatars - and it's canonically a strong enough push that they just can't be good people. That's not contradictory with the idea that they can have <i>other</i> goals<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To a Nephandus who is seeking to destroy the universe, selling their soul to a demon lord is simply a means to an end. </div> </div> </div>That is what some say on Infernalism. However that same book went on about how they actually don't like to sell their souls to a &quot;lesser evil&quot; like demon lords.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The consequences of such a choice are ultimately irrelevant, since there won't be a Hell, once they reduce everything back to the cosmic void from whence it came. </div> </div> </div>Nephandi don't seem to be too keen on avoiding Hell out of fear, tho. At least one third of them wanted a Hell on Earth. They do seem to want privileges, tho. But I think that's their humanity talking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Nephandus can traffic with demons, and engage in all manner of horrific atrocities, without fear of reprisal, because there won't be anyone left to reprise them when all is said and done. </div> </div> </div>This would be a tremedously ingenuous belief. Nephandi plan for the long run, they know they can get trapped into hell far before anything of that gets done. Only stupid Nephandi would deal with a demon lord thinking they aren't going to end in hell.<br /> <br /> A different thing it's if they care - as they sometimes don't seem to care. But there doesn't seem to be an &quot;easy way out&quot; rationale behind that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T14:30:02-07:00","id":1563962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563957#post1563957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Observation: any theory where you end up as a creator god if your own universe must be balanced against the fact that you'll do so only after being exposed to constant suffering to an absolutely unhealthy point, so it's possible that your godlike self will be too deranged and emotionally pathetic to be able to create anything that actually improves their lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, come on!<br /> <br /> &quot;Suffering breeds character!&quot; and all that nonsense.<br /> <br /> But yes, I misunderstood their intentions behind not creating a Player's Guide for the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T14:35:13-07:00","id":1563963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563958#post1563958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is pointless because nobody said that Nephandi can't strive for something else. </div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, quite a lot of people told me they couldn't. I believe it was stated earlier that only one faction of the Nephandi have openly admitted to be after universal dissolvement, while every other faction has their minds set on other goals. Yet pointing this out was met with arguments to the contrary, about how the inverted Avatars will urge the Nephandi towards mindless destruction, regardless of their desires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T17:30:34-07:00","id":1563967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563963#post1563963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the inverted Avatars will urge the Nephandi towards mindless destruction, regardless of their desires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not mindless. <i>Exhaustive.</i> From a rational point of view, that seems mindless, because if the Nephandi succeed, retroactively everything ever will have been pointless.<br /> <br /> So why are they so committed to it? Young and/or stupid ones just don't think that hard about it. They are, to borrow from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>, posuers. The deep Nephandi, though, they understand it and are here for it. They know that <i>literally anything other than their success would be better for literally everyone BY DEFINITION</i>, <i>and they're working toward it anyway</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 09-11-2026, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T20:27:05-07:00","id":1563971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563963#post1563963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, quite a lot of people told me they couldn't. I believe it was stated earlier that only one faction of the Nephandi have openly admitted to be after universal dissolvement, while every other faction has their minds set on other goals. Yet pointing this out was met with arguments to the contrary, about how the inverted Avatars will urge the Nephandi towards mindless destruction, regardless of their desires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify here, what we meant is that Nefandi can't strive for something else <i>meaningfully</i>. This last part does a lot of heavy lifting.<br /> <br /> The character can strive for more, just like everyone else. The problems are tangential, but many and compound quick and heavily, though:<br /> <br /> 1. Your Avatar don't care and is way more aggressive than a regular Avatar. It may use your ambition as a means to manipulate you at first, but it doesn't really care and won't suffer your ambition getting in the way, period.<br /> <br /> 2. Your society doesn't care, either. Literally. They are too nihilistic to give a damn to your ambition and if you succeed or not. They don't want a piece of your power and don't envy or fear you for it. They only care for you as force of continuous corruption or victim.<br /> <br /> 3. Your patrons don't care. They won't give you a pat in the back for grabing power. You make no difference, your personal success doesn't either. You work just fine as king or beggar, and when they need a king they have enough options, so you're not impressing them no matter how grandiose your achievements.<br /> <br /> 4. Big problem: building anything, even if evil, means working for stability, consistent results, making your assets valuable, etc. Having an ambition besides mere nihilistic misanthropic vengeance kind of requires creative goals. The higher ups in the Nefandi don't have much of a tolerance for creative goals.<br /> <br /> Bottom line: if chasing an ambition keeps you running for them, Nefandi and their patrons will let you have all your complex motivations, sure. The problem is that as soon as your ambition clashes with their agenda you'll find out it was never a negotiation, they don't compromise and your personal desires don't matter.<br /> <br /> So your character can <i>have</i> other goals. It's the notion that being a Nefandus will <i>work</i> as a means to an end that's wrong, not because the character doesn't think like that, but because they're wrong and will find out how thoroughly the Descension controls their lifes.<br /> <br /> One way to think about it is that you struck a bargain for power and support, and several others did... But you found out all the miriad organizations recruiting people were actually run by the Joker and he planted a bomb in your brain surgically. You're not necessarily devoid of self awareness, although most in your situation are, because Joker, but awareness and ambition won't change the orders coming from the Joker while you have a bomb in your brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T22:17:26-07:00","id":1563976,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Is it possible for an Avatar to effectively 'go back to sleep' or just stop empowering a mage, if they decide to rebel against it? I'm a bit confused as to whether or not your Avatar is supposed to be a separate entity, or a manifestation of the mage's soul.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, I understand they can't seek out something meaningful. I wasn't clear enough in explaining that. What I meant was that the other factions seem to be more preoccupied with indulging themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Infernalists</b> (Nephandi version) are described as trying to achieve world domination, using demons as tools and servants to accomplish that.<br /> <br /> <b>Goat Kids</b> are a hedonistic cult, that revels in debauchery as they perform blasphemous rituals in the name of their dark patrons.<br /> <br /> <b>Mammonites</b> are blindly obsessed with increasing their profit margins, and have absolutely no moral scruples about how they go about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-11T00:08:08-07:00","id":1563977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563976#post1563976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Is it possible for an Avatar to effectively 'go back to sleep' or just stop empowering a mage, if they decide to rebel against it? I'm a bit confused as to whether or not your Avatar is supposed to be a separate entity, or a manifestation of the mage's soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Avatars are an active mystery in the setting, a big one at that. So how much they're a part of the Mage in a metaphysical sense is uncertain.<br /> <br /> But for practical purpose it's a distinct entity. It has as its goal the Mage's Awakening, Seeking and Ascension, but otherwise thinks and acts on its own, through its own strategies, and can even be bad at its work.<br /> <br /> So we have examples of everything. Avatars that go back to Sleep are rare, but happens. An Avatar is unlikely to do that due to differences in approach, but may do so if the Mage is too depressed or disinterested to the point of actively avoiding everything about Magic. Or just been too damaged by stacked brainwashing, IME.<br /> <br /> Rebellious Avatars are more common and their Mages wish they would just stop empowering Magic... As an Avatar can do literally anything. The most common situation is an Avatar being a jerk in the Mages Dreams, sending constant signs and whatnot, but some Avatars do things like attract your enemies or change reality to bring problems your way, hijack your senses so you're suddenly blind to the world while trapped in a reality of their doing, sell secrets to opposing factions that will force you to stop waiting and do something about it.<br /> <br /> While the apex of their power and specialized strategy is being discreet to the world around, acting as if they were just an inner voice, some Avatars just materialize and dirt their hands with your blood for good measure. Against the Mage the Avatar doesn't even roll dice. They do what they want, period. But even with others, while rare there are records of a Mage's Avatar just materializing, invading the Chantry and proceeding to beat the hell up of the whole Cabal.<br /> <br /> Inverted Avatars are considerably more willing to go to such extremes. Most Mages won't ever see evidence that their Avatars aren't just their imagination (they know, they've been informed of it, but don't see actual evidence), with very few facing it in direct conflict of any kind. But a Nefandus Avatar will be an abusive taskmaster at best, and cause mental illness regularly even for fun. And yes, it's still rare, but if needed the nuclear option of just beating the crap out of the Mage is still there.<br /> <br /> On the problem with their personal goals, it goes like that:<br /> <br /> Infernalists want world domination and overall personal power, and the devils they bargain with offer as much. But in the end those devils use the chains of the pacts to demand greater and greater evil, even if it means destroying the power base just built. They use the demons, the demons use them, but the Mages notice too late that despite their best efforts they are in a hugely weaker position in the negotiation.<br /> <br /> Goat Kids are idiotic edge lords. And like most idiotic edge lords they'll find out with time that doing only that every day, all the time, gets old fast. This is when they notice that they made a permanent arrangement for a passing fancy, even if this fancy was more remarkable than usual. Things worth keeping come, interesting opportunities for the future show up, relational attachments form, and you have to just keep breaking everything and indulge the next blood orgy, that's just like dozens of previous ones.<br /> <br /> Mammonites face a two-layer problem. One is when their patrons demand risk or sacrifice of the very wealth they wanted in some way, be it asking to employ it in the service of evil or to just manage your money with inefficient excess evil. But the other is that being criminal all the time means leaving liabilities all the time and owing favors to the wrong people, so they always have a lot of people with dirt on them that can harm their fortune a lot.<br /> <br /> All of them with time will find out that the scope of the bargain doesn't really mesh with the very concept of wanting something for yourself, even if their goals and your wants at first look compatible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-11T05:29:36-07:00","id":1563982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563963#post1563963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, quite a lot of people told me they couldn't. I believe it was stated earlier that only one faction of the Nephandi have openly admitted to be after universal dissolvement, while every other faction has their minds set on other goals. Yet pointing this out was met with arguments to the contrary, about how the inverted Avatars will urge the Nephandi towards mindless destruction, regardless of their desires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inverted Avatars WILL urge the Nephandi towards mindless destruction, regardless of their desires.<br /> <br /> That's a force stripping them of freedom, but not a <i>logical contradiction</i> to freedom. See the difference?<br /> <br /> Greedy Syndicate agents can polute, exploit and enslave people, and proffit from crime of the worst kinds. None of this it's described as distinct of Nephandi. They even have a sanctioned Procedure to extract the life force of exploited workers on a sweatshop to get extra Quintessence...that's <i>not</i> against the Protocols<br /> <br /> What's the difference between such a vile Syndicate agent and a Mammonite? : The Syndicate agent does evil deeds because he's greedy, the Nephandi doesn't do evil deeds <i>because</i> he's greedy, but rather it's <i>urged</i> to do evil <i>regardless</i> of greed, he just can't opperate otherwise.<br /> <br /> You could guide the vile Syndicate agent towards doing good appealing to potential gains, you can't do that so easily with the Nephandus - he may be greedy, but he's evil first and foremost and would need to figth his inverted Avatar to become a force of constructive good even for greed's sake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it possible for an Avatar to effectively 'go back to sleep' or just stop empowering a mage, if they decide to rebel against it? I'm a bit confused as to whether or not your Avatar is supposed to be a separate entity, or a manifestation of the mage's soul. </div> </div> </div>Avatars can do all sort of things, even magick. That doesn't mean they're a sepparate entity, this is unknown - but they can and do enter in conflict with their mages.<br /> <br /> It's unknown how Inverted Avatars force their mages to do stuff, but, as said they're a strong enough influence that Nephandi just <i>can't</i> be good people. Not even under the effects of Conditioning.<br /> That's a LOT more than your regular Avatar. <hr /><br /> Nothing of this makes Nephandi *technically* unplayable, but it does generate some problems:<br /> <br /> *They're uninteresting to the point not a single one of the proposed &quot;player characters&quot; here gains anything from being a Nephandus. Their goals and the way they're evil simply doesn't give Nephandic &quot;vives&quot; to me - of course they <i>could</i> be Nephandi, as any bad guy can, but there's nothing in the way they were portrayed here that indicates to me that they <i>are </i>Nephandi. That would require giving a spin to their story where this ... &quot;<i>background noise of cosmic nihilism</i>&quot; ... everyone it's mentioning to you it's taken in count.<br /> <br /> *They're problematic as PC. They're poor teamplayers that will work towards destroying the other PC. Unless they're all Nephandi (in that case you can apply the Skeletor meme: Joke's on you, I'm into that shit) Even then they would need some solid reasons to not throw each other under the bus at the chance of gaining something from it.<br /> <br /> Also a story of Nephandi would almost necessarily involve debasing your setting as a short/long term goal (even if your setting was <i>evil by desing</i>, the story would have to be about making it <i>worse</i>) - and I don't see myself narrating such a story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-11-2026, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-11T11:47:38-07:00","id":1563983,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Okay, the idea of an Avatar just beating the crap out of their mage and going through a step by step breakdown of where they went wrong is amusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T09:57:00-07:00","id":1564018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1563957#post1563957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Observation: any theory where you end up as a creator god if your own universe must be balanced against the fact that you'll do so only after being exposed to constant suffering to an absolutely unhealthy point, so it's possible that your godlike self will be too deranged and emotionally pathetic to be able to create anything that actually improves their lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>This got me thinking. However improbable or difficult, would it at least be possible for a Mage, as part of an elaborate but genuinely altruistic scheme to save/rebuild the world, to go Nephandus for access to their world-ending power, if he thought another Mage he trusted implicitly could take advantage of the last nearly-formless moments of Reality to catalyze a new and better one?<br /> <br /> Obviously his Avatar would have none of it, so it would probably take (at least) powerful Mind magic or the like to compartmentalize or excise the parts of him that knew it was an attempted double-cross. And because of that, the resulting Nephandus could *not* be counted on to pull punches or otherwise aid his trustee of his own volition. But maybe he could bind himself ahead of time in ways that would make him somewhat less efficient? What would it take to wipe the Avatar's memory?<br /> <br /> For all purposes the Nephandus is still a Nephandus and will act, think, etc like one; you could say he's not even the same Mage, just one who has been manipulated(/sacrificed) by the Mage he used to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T10:33:10-07:00","id":1564019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1564018#post1564018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This got me thinking. However improbable or difficult, would it at least be possible for a Mage, as part of an elaborate but genuinely altruistic scheme to save/rebuild the world, to go Nephandus for access to their world-ending power, if he thought another Mage he trusted implicitly could take advantage of the last nearly-formless moments of Reality to catalyze a new and better one?<br /> <br /> Obviously his Avatar would have none of it, so it would probably take (at least) powerful Mind magic or the like to compartmentalize or excise the parts of him that knew it was an attempted double-cross. And because of that, the resulting Nephandus could *not* be counted on to pull punches or otherwise aid his trustee of his own volition. But maybe he could bind himself ahead of time in ways that would make him somewhat less efficient? What would it take to wipe the Avatar's memory?<br /> <br /> For all purposes the Nephandus is still a Nephandus and will act, think, etc like one; you could say he's not even the same Mage, just one who has been manipulated(/sacrificed) by the Mage he used to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I'm aware, that plan would be doomed before it even started.<br /> <br /> The Nephandus would die in their Caul, if they were not 100% willingly committed to serving the cause of evil for its own sake.<br /> <br /> Attempting to trick or manipulate the forces of darkness, while actually striving to achieve a greater good would result in the process failing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T17:56:12-07:00","id":1564025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1564018#post1564018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This got me thinking. However improbable or difficult, would it at least be possible for a Mage, as part of an elaborate but genuinely altruistic scheme to save/rebuild the world, to go Nephandus for access to their world-ending power, if he thought another Mage he trusted implicitly could take advantage of the last nearly-formless moments of Reality to catalyze a new and better one?<br /> <br /> Obviously his Avatar would have none of it, so it would probably take (at least) powerful Mind magic or the like to compartmentalize or excise the parts of him that knew it was an attempted double-cross. And because of that, the resulting Nephandus could *not* be counted on to pull punches or otherwise aid his trustee of his own volition. But maybe he could bind himself ahead of time in ways that would make him somewhat less efficient? What would it take to wipe the Avatar's memory?<br /> <br /> For all purposes the Nephandus is still a Nephandus and will act, think, etc like one; you could say he's not even the same Mage, just one who has been manipulated(/sacrificed) by the Mage he used to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible? Yes. How truly good is their plan, morally speaking, is for another time, but I do think it is feasible.<br /> <br /> The tricky part would be to fool the Avatar, that would require Spirit 5 at least, and the risk is that it's hard to know what resources an Avatar doesn't have to restore itself from a &quot;minor&quot; alteration of memory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1564019#post1564019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I'm aware, that plan would be doomed before it even started.<br /> <br /> The Nephandus would die in their Caul, if they were not 100% willingly committed to serving the cause of evil for its own sake.<br /> <br /> Attempting to trick or manipulate the forces of darkness, while actually striving to achieve a greater good would result in the process failing.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a chance, slim as it is. Just requires enough Mind Magic.<br /> <br /> Basically the idea is to split the mind several times to isolate the plan and the thoughts that birthed it, while rewiring the rest with substitute thoughts that nudge it in the right mindset with no direct imposition.<br /> <br /> It's a very complicated process with high risks involved, but has been specifically researched for a long time, so it's actually not an unknown method. Ridiculously risky and prone to fail in spectacular fashion, but still well mapped, just enough crazy people did it in the past.<br /> <br /> Your result is basically a new person, though, derived from the original. And the safest route to complete the plan is to make the original irrecoverable. Also requires a lot understanding of people, because the new persona must emerge with minimal intervention to ensure it will work unnoticed.<br /> <br /> At the end the Mage so transformed sacrificed themselves utterly to create an actual, true to heard Nefandus with a hidden weakness to be explored later. This future Nefandus, by the way, must be made genuinely competent and unrepentant. The level of risk involved is just insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T20:23:06-07:00","id":1564033,"title":"","content":"Note I never said it was a <i>good</i> plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T09:32:25-07:00","id":1564046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1564019#post1564019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nephandus would die in their Caul, if they were not 100% willingly committed to serving the cause of evil for its own sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that's not true. Whilst <i>Book of the Fallen</i> does state that, I'd note that it's a Nephandi saying it. The only concrete statement I can see is that a totally unwilling person gets minced by the cauls.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile we have quite a few examples to the contrary. The Ahl-i-Batin in particular are noted for thinking they were too pure for the cauls and ending up as Nephandi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T20:50:28-07:00","id":1564064,"title":"","content":"You know, having a mage who hived off part of their mind/Avatar to enact such a long-term plan would be an interesting explanation for having the Shattered Avatar merit. The PC inherited the untainted part (or one of them, if the original mage was hedging their bets), while a Widderslainte is born with (one of?) the other part(s?).<br /> <br /> Heck, even if there isn't a long-term plan here, a Shattered Avatar might represent the result of a bygone mage seeing their fall coming, and breaking their Avatar into pieces simply to kneecap their post-Caul self. Limit the amount of damage they can do by curtailing their spiritual power. (So their Nephandus successor only has Avatar 0-1, while the other parts are scattered elsewhere).<br /> <br /> In any event, one must then question what would happen if one holder of the Shattered Avatar claimed a shard held by the Nephandus, or vice versa. Would/could the spiritual inversion be healed if forcibly integrated in an &quot;untainted&quot; Avatar? Would the presence of the inverted shard corrupt the untainted, simply by its presence? Would it be a matter of which side had a higher Avatar rating (so, an Avatar 3 normal shard would &quot;overpower&quot; an Avatar 1 Nephandus shard)? Or would it be a matter of Willpower; a contest of Wills to see whether light or darkness won?<br /> <br /> Honestly, you could build a whole chronicle out of this. Or at least a chronicle-spanning character arc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T20:59:46-07:00","id":1564065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1564064#post1564064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any event, one must then question what would happen if one holder of the Shattered Avatar claimed a shard held by the Nephandus, or vice versa. Would/could the spiritual inversion be healed if forcibly integrated in an &quot;untainted&quot; Avatar? Would the presence of the inverted shard corrupt the untainted, simply by its presence? Would it be a matter of which side had a higher Avatar rating (so, an Avatar 3 normal shard would &quot;overpower&quot; an Avatar 1 Nephandus shard)? Or would it be a matter of Willpower; a contest of Wills to see whether light or darkness won?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe there's a Sphere the mage can never seem to learn; after recovering the shard they find they can... but it's Qlippothic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T23:09:33-07:00","id":1564066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1564064#post1564064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any event, one must then question what would happen if one holder of the Shattered Avatar claimed a shard held by the Nephandus, or vice versa. Would/could the spiritual inversion be healed if forcibly integrated in an &quot;untainted&quot; Avatar? Would the presence of the inverted shard corrupt the untainted, simply by its presence? Would it be a matter of which side had a higher Avatar rating (so, an Avatar 3 normal shard would &quot;overpower&quot; an Avatar 1 Nephandus shard)? Or would it be a matter of Willpower; a contest of Wills to see whether light or darkness won?<br /> <br /> Honestly, you could build a whole chronicle out of this. Or at least a chronicle-spanning character arc...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shaving off pieces of a corrupted soul and placing them inside somebody else didn't work out so well for a certain snake faced wizard.<br /> <br /> Even if it were theoretically possible to heal the physical aspect, the mental damage would be ever lasting.<br /> <br /> You don't just shrug off being metaphysically turned inside out and then getting put right side in again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T12:39:02-07:00","id":1564247,"title":"","content":"I've played Nephandi.<br /> <br /> It only lasted two sessions because everyone involved had their own idea how to run a super evil badguy wizard but it was fun while it lasted.<br /> <br /> I think you run into the same problem as if you try to run an Evil aligned campaign in DND. You can't just say 'you play evil badguys' you need to specify if we're going hellraiser or Hannibal lecter or batman the animated series or something else. Evil is a matter of genre.<br /> <br /> Also need to be clear on how much and what sort of pvp is on the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T13:53:36-07:00","id":1564254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1557471-nephandi-are-not-playable-except-they-are?p=1564247#post1564247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You can't just say 'you play evil badguys' you need to specify if we're going hellraiser</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just a follower of <b>Loviatar / Zon-Kuthon.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T08:28:26-07:00","id":1564272,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It only lasted two sessions because everyone involved had their own idea how to run a super evil badguy wizard but it was fun while it lasted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least it's good for One Shots <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> More seriously, the table not being able to &quot;survive&quot; <i>two </i>sessions of being Nephandi (due to fictional problems rather than real life problems) ... it's pretty bad ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Evil is a matter of genre.<br /> <br /> Also need to be clear on how much and what sort of pvp is on the table. </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It seems that such a RP experience needs stricter &quot;convivence rules&quot; than average if one doesn't want the group to implode. Can't leave anything to 'vives' nor assume everyone it's going to play nice, even if they normaly do.<br /> <br /> Tools like the X card could be more powerful and important here than on average. I've never used these tools, but I wouldn't risk <i>this one </i>to run on my empathy as ST. Everyone agreeing on using a &quot;lifeline&quot; to get out of the experience and change the approach if someone isn't having fun sounds like a mentality that could save the table ... maybe.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T12:44:16-07:00","id":1564275,"title":"","content":"A one shot is a really good idea for trying things out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T16:08:09-07:00","id":1564282,"title":"","content":"One shots, sure.<br /> <br /> As for a chronicle, resources like the X card would be good not just because of general psychological safety, but as management tools for conflicts that can generate Out of Character frustration.<br /> <br /> Probably a tight control at character creation will also help, I'd say making the group together around agreed upon common elements and goals is desirable.<br /> <br /> It's still a very specific kind of chronicle, and it may not be too long lived just because of how destructive it can get, but with preparation it may survive more than half a dozen sessions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}